(window.LMT_ARTICLES = window.LMT_ARTICLES || {})["timemap"] = [{"id":"gregorian-1582-ten-days","icon":"✂️","tags":["gregorian calendar","julian calendar","calendar reform","easter","britain"],"title":{"en":"Ten Days Cut from October 1582","ja":"1582年10月、消えた10日間","ko":"1582년 10월에서 사라진 열흘","zh":"1582年10月被删去的十天","yue":"1582年10月憑空消失嘅十日","vi":"Mười ngày bị cắt khỏi tháng Mười năm 1582","th":"สิบวันที่หายไปจากเดือนตุลาคม ค.ศ. 1582","id":"Sepuluh Hari yang Dipangkas dari Oktober 1582","hi":"अक्टूबर 1582 से काटे गए दस दिन","de":"Zehn Tage, die im Oktober 1582 wegfielen","fr":"Dix jours retranchés en octobre 1582","it":"Dieci giorni tolti all'ottobre del 1582","es":"Diez días suprimidos en octubre de 1582","pt":"Dez dias cortados de outubro de 1582","ru":"Десять дней, вырезанных из октября 1582 года","uk":"Десять днів, вирізаних із жовтня 1582 року","ar":"عشرة أيام حُذفت من أكتوبر 1582","he":"עשרה ימים שנגזרו מאוקטובר 1582","sw":"Siku Kumi Zilizoondolewa Oktoba 1582"},"summary":{"en":"Under Pope Gregory XIII's bull of 1582, Friday 15 October followed Thursday 4 October. Britain did not switch until 1752, and the riots said to have followed are a later myth.","ja":"グレゴリウス13世の1582年の勅書により、10月4日（木）の翌日は10月15日（金）になった。イギリスの切り替えは1752年で、そのとき起きたとされる暴動は後世の作り話である。","ko":"교황 그레고리오 13세의 1582년 교서에 따라 10월 4일 목요일 다음 날이 10월 15일 금요일이 되었다. 영국은 1752년에야 역법을 바꾸었고, 그 뒤에 일어났다는 폭동은 후대에 생긴 속설이다.","zh":"根据教宗格里高利十三世1582年颁布的诏书，10月4日星期四的次日就是10月15日星期五。英国直到1752年才改历，而所谓改历后爆发的骚乱，是后人编出来的说法。","yue":"根據教宗格里高利十三世喺1582年頒布嘅詔書，10月4號星期四嘅第二日就係10月15號星期五。英國要到1752年先改曆，至於之後話有暴動，其實係後人作出嚟嘅講法。","vi":"Theo sắc chỉ năm 1582 của Giáo hoàng Grêgôriô XIII, liền sau thứ Năm ngày 4 tháng 10 là thứ Sáu ngày 15 tháng 10. Nước Anh mãi đến năm 1752 mới đổi lịch, còn chuyện bạo loạn được cho là nổ ra sau đó chỉ là huyền thoại có về sau.","th":"ตามพระสมณโองการปี 1582 ของสมเด็จพระสันตะปาปาเกรกอรีที่ 13 วันถัดจากวันพฤหัสบดีที่ 4 ตุลาคมคือวันศุกร์ที่ 15 ตุลาคม บริเตนไม่ได้เปลี่ยนจนถึงปี 1752 และเรื่องจลาจลที่เล่ากันว่าเกิดตามมานั้นเป็นตำนานที่เกิดขึ้นภายหลัง","id":"Berdasarkan bula Paus Gregorius XIII tahun 1582, Kamis 4 Oktober langsung disusul Jumat 15 Oktober. Britania Raya baru beralih pada 1752, dan kerusuhan yang konon menyusulnya hanyalah mitos yang muncul belakangan.","hi":"पोप ग्रेगरी तेरहवें के 1582 के बुल के तहत गुरुवार 4 अक्टूबर के बाद सीधे शुक्रवार 15 अक्टूबर आया। ब्रिटेन ने यह बदलाव 1752 तक नहीं अपनाया, और उसके बाद हुए बताए जाने वाले दंगे बाद में गढ़ा गया मिथक हैं।","de":"Nach der Bulle Papst Gregors XIII. von 1582 folgte auf Donnerstag, den 4. Oktober, Freitag, der 15. Oktober. Großbritannien stellte erst 1752 um, und die angeblich darauf folgenden Unruhen sind eine spätere Legende.","fr":"En vertu de la bulle du pape Grégoire XIII de 1582, le vendredi 15 octobre succéda au jeudi 4 octobre. La Grande-Bretagne ne changea qu'en 1752, et les émeutes qui auraient suivi relèvent d'un mythe plus tardif.","it":"In base alla bolla di papa Gregorio XIII del 1582, a giovedì 4 ottobre seguì venerdì 15 ottobre. La Gran Bretagna cambiò solo nel 1752, e le sommosse che ne sarebbero seguite sono un mito posteriore.","es":"Según la bula de 1582 del papa Gregorio XIII, al jueves 4 de octubre le siguió el viernes 15 de octubre. Gran Bretaña no hizo el cambio hasta 1752, y los disturbios que supuestamente le siguieron son un mito posterior.","pt":"Pela bula de 1582 do papa Gregório XIII, a sexta-feira, 15 de outubro, veio logo depois da quinta-feira, 4 de outubro. A Grã-Bretanha só mudou em 1752, e os tumultos que teriam ocorrido em seguida são um mito posterior.","ru":"По булле папы Григория XIII 1582 года за четвергом 4 октября сразу последовала пятница 15 октября. Британия перешла на новый календарь лишь в 1752 году, а будто бы вспыхнувшие тогда бунты — позднейший миф.","uk":"За буллою папи Григорія XIII 1582 року після четверга 4 жовтня одразу настала п'ятниця 15 жовтня. Британія перейшла на новий календар лише 1752 року, а заворушення, які нібито тоді спалахнули, — пізніший міф.","ar":"بموجب المرسوم البابوي الذي أصدره البابا غريغوريوس الثالث عشر عام 1582، جاء يوم الجمعة 15 أكتوبر بعد يوم الخميس 4 أكتوبر مباشرة. ولم تتحوّل بريطانيا إلى التقويم الجديد إلا عام 1752، أما أعمال الشغب التي يُقال إنها أعقبت ذلك فأسطورة نشأت لاحقًا.","he":"לפי הבולה של האפיפיור גרגוריוס ה־13 משנת 1582, אחרי יום חמישי, 4 באוקטובר, בא מיד יום שישי, 15 באוקטובר. בריטניה עברה ללוח החדש רק ב־1752, והמהומות שפרצו כביכול בעקבות זאת הן מיתוס מאוחר.","sw":"Chini ya hati ya Papa Gregori XIII ya mwaka 1582, Ijumaa tarehe 15 Oktoba ilifuata Alhamisi tarehe 4 Oktoba. Uingereza haikubadili hadi 1752, na ghasia zinazodaiwa kufuata ni hadithi ya kubuni iliyozuka baadaye."},"body":{"en":"<h3>4 October, then 15 October</h3><p>In the Papal States and most of Catholic Italy, and in Spain, Portugal and Poland-Lithuania, Thursday 4 October 1582 was followed by Friday 15 October. The ten dates in between were never used there. The weekdays ran on as before (Thursday was still followed by Friday), so only the day of the month jumped. The order came from Pope Gregory XIII's bull <em>Inter gravissimas</em>, signed at Tusculum (Frascati) on what we now call 24 February 1582. The bull's own dating clause says 1581, because it counts the year of the Incarnation from 25 March. France followed two months later, going straight from 9 to 20 December 1582.</p><h3>Eleven minutes a year</h3><p>The Julian calendar, in force since 45 BC, adds a leap day every fourth year, which makes the average year 365.25 days. The tropical year, from one spring equinox to the next, is about 365.2422 days. The Julian year is therefore about 11 minutes too long, and the calendar date of the equinox moves one day earlier roughly every 128 years. By 1582 the spring equinox fell on about 11 March.</p><p>The drift mattered because of Easter, which falls on the Sunday after the first full moon on or after the spring equinox. The Church's tables fixed that equinox at 21 March. The bull states that the fathers of the Council of Nicaea had set the equinox on 21 March (in Roman terms, the twelfth day before the Kalends of April), though the council's surviving documents do not give that date. The reform set out to put the equinox back on 21 March. That is why it removed ten days rather than thirteen: it restored the sky of AD 325, not the sky of Julius Caesar's time.</p><h3>The new leap-year rule</h3><p>To stop the drift recurring, the bull kept a leap day every fourth year but dropped it in century years not divisible by 400. In its own words, 1700, 1800 and 1900 would not be leap years, while 1600 and 2000 would. Removing three leap days every 400 years gives an average year of 365.2425 days, about 27 seconds longer than the tropical year. The scheme was devised by the Calabrian physician Aloysius Lilius (Luigi Lilio), who died in 1576. The Jesuit mathematician Christopher Clavius then defended and explained it in print.</p><h3>Britain, 1752</h3><p>Most Protestant states changed later. Great Britain and its colonies switched under the Calendar (New Style) Act 1750: Wednesday 2 September 1752 was followed by Thursday 14 September. By then the gap was eleven days, not ten, because 1700 had been a leap year under the Julian rule but not under the Gregorian one. The same act moved the start of the year in England, Wales, Ireland and the colonies from 25 March to 1 January, so 1751 there ran only from 25 March to 31 December. George Washington was born in Virginia on 11 February 1731 by the old reckoning. Under the new style that date is 22 February 1732.</p><p>The British tax year still shows the join. It had begun on Lady Day, 25 March. To keep a full year's revenue, its start was moved eleven days on, to 5 April. In 1800, a leap year in the old calendar but not the new, it moved again, to 6 April, which is still the first day of the UK tax year.</p><h3>“Give us our Eleven Days”</h3><p>The story that crowds rioted in 1752 to demand their eleven days back has no contemporary support. In a 1995 article in <em>Past &amp; Present</em>, the historian Robert Poole traced the story mainly to William Hogarth's painting <em>An Election Entertainment</em> (c. 1755). The painting shows a Whig dinner during the bitterly fought Oxfordshire election of 1754. In the lower right lies a captured Tory banner reading “Give us our Eleven Days”. One of the Whig candidates was Viscount Parker, son of the Earl of Macclesfield, an astronomer who had helped push the act through. The calendar was one of the charges his opponents used against him. Later writers took the election joke for a record of mob violence.</p><p>On the map, the Vatican's Gregorian label first appears on 15 October 1582 and the British one on 14 September 1752. On those two days the Julian calendar, still kept by the Russian Orthodox Church, reads 5 October and 3 September.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1582-10-15\" data-cal=\"greg_va\">📅 15 October 1582 in Rome</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1752-09-14\" data-cal=\"greg_uk\">📅 14 September 1752 in Britain</button></div>"},"sources":[{"text":"Gregory XIII, Inter gravissimas (bull, 24 February 1582), English translation by Bill Spencer from the Latin and French of Rodolphe Audette, 1999/2002","url":"https://www.bluewaterarts.com/calendar/NewInterGravissimas.htm"},{"text":"Calendar (New Style) Act 1750 (24 Geo. 2 c. 23), legislation.gov.uk, The National Archives","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/apgb/Geo2/24/23"},{"text":"Robert Poole, 1995, \"'Give us our eleven days!': Calendar Reform in Eighteenth-Century England\", Past & Present 149: 95–139, Oxford University Press","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/past/149.1.95"},{"text":"Historic UK, \"Give Us Our Eleven Days\" (Hogarth's An Election Entertainment; the tax year moving to 5 and then 6 April)","url":"https://www.historic-uk.com/HistoryUK/HistoryofBritain/Give-us-our-eleven-days/"}]},{"id":"russia-october-in-november","icon":"🚩","tags":["julian calendar","gregorian calendar","russia","orthodox church","calendar reform"],"title":{"en":"The October Revolution in November","ja":"11月に起きた十月革命","ko":"11월에 일어난 10월 혁명","zh":"发生在十一月的十月革命","yue":"喺十一月發生嘅十月革命","vi":"Cách mạng Tháng Mười diễn ra vào tháng Mười một","th":"การปฏิวัติเดือนตุลาคมที่เกิดในเดือนพฤศจิกายน","id":"Revolusi Oktober di Bulan November","hi":"नवंबर में अक्टूबर क्रांति","de":"Die Oktoberrevolution im November","fr":"La révolution d'Octobre en novembre","it":"La Rivoluzione d'Ottobre a novembre","es":"La Revolución de Octubre en noviembre","pt":"A Revolução de Outubro em novembro","ru":"Октябрьская революция в ноябре","uk":"Жовтнева революція в листопаді","ar":"ثورة أكتوبر في نوفمبر","he":"מהפכת אוקטובר בנובמבר","sw":"Mapinduzi ya Oktoba mwezi Novemba"},"summary":{"en":"Russia's revolution took place on 25 October 1917 in the Julian calendar, which was 7 November in the Gregorian. Soviet Russia switched in February 1918, Greece in 1923, and the Russian Church never did. After 2100 the gap grows to 14 days.","ja":"ロシア革命はユリウス暦で1917年10月25日、グレゴリオ暦では11月7日に起きた。ソビエト・ロシアは1918年2月に暦を切り替え、ギリシャは1923年に続いたが、ロシア正教会は今もユリウス暦を使っている。2100年を過ぎると、二つの暦の差は14日に広がる。","ko":"러시아 혁명은 율리우스력으로 1917년 10월 25일, 그레고리력으로는 11월 7일에 일어났다. 소비에트 러시아는 1918년 2월, 그리스는 1923년에 역법을 바꿨지만 러시아 정교회는 끝내 바꾸지 않았다. 2100년이 지나면 그 차이는 14일로 벌어진다.","zh":"俄国革命发生在儒略历1917年10月25日，即格里高利历11月7日。苏维埃俄国于1918年2月改历，希腊于1923年改历，而俄罗斯东正教会始终没有改。2100年以后，两历相差将扩大到14天。","yue":"俄國革命發生喺儒略曆1917年10月25日，即係格里曆11月7日。蘇維埃俄國喺1918年2月改曆，希臘喺1923年改，而俄羅斯東正教會就一直冇改。2100年之後，兩套曆法嘅差距會擴大到14日。","vi":"Cuộc cách mạng ở Nga diễn ra ngày 25 tháng 10 năm 1917 theo lịch Julius, tức ngày 7 tháng 11 theo lịch Gregory. Nước Nga Xô viết đổi lịch vào tháng 2 năm 1918, Hy Lạp vào năm 1923, còn Giáo hội Nga thì không bao giờ đổi. Sau năm 2100, khoảng cách sẽ tăng lên 14 ngày.","th":"การปฏิวัติรัสเซียเกิดขึ้นวันที่ 25 ตุลาคม 1917 ตามปฏิทินจูเลียน ซึ่งตรงกับวันที่ 7 พฤศจิกายนตามปฏิทินเกรกอเรียน รัสเซียโซเวียตเปลี่ยนปฏิทินในเดือนกุมภาพันธ์ 1918 กรีซเปลี่ยนในปี 1923 ส่วนคริสตจักรรัสเซียไม่เคยเปลี่ยนเลย หลังปี 2100 ส่วนต่างจะเพิ่มเป็น 14 วัน","id":"Revolusi Rusia terjadi pada 25 Oktober 1917 menurut kalender Julian, yaitu 7 November menurut kalender Gregorian. Rusia Soviet beralih pada Februari 1918, Yunani pada 1923, sedangkan Gereja Rusia tidak pernah beralih. Setelah 2100 selisihnya menjadi 14 hari.","hi":"रूस की क्रांति जूलियन कैलेंडर के अनुसार 25 अक्टूबर 1917 को हुई थी, जो ग्रेगोरियन कैलेंडर में 7 नवंबर था। सोवियत रूस ने फ़रवरी 1918 में कैलेंडर बदला, यूनान ने 1923 में, और रूसी चर्च ने कभी नहीं बदला। 2100 के बाद यह अंतर बढ़कर 14 दिन हो जाएगा।","de":"Die russische Revolution fand am 25. Oktober 1917 nach dem julianischen Kalender statt, nach dem gregorianischen am 7. November. Sowjetrussland stellte im Februar 1918 um, Griechenland 1923, die Russische Kirche nie. Nach 2100 wächst der Abstand auf 14 Tage.","fr":"La révolution russe a eu lieu le 25 octobre 1917 selon le calendrier julien, soit le 7 novembre dans le grégorien. La Russie soviétique a changé en février 1918, la Grèce en 1923, et l'Église russe jamais. Après 2100, l'écart passera à 14 jours.","it":"La rivoluzione russa avvenne il 25 ottobre 1917 secondo il calendario giuliano, cioè il 7 novembre in quello gregoriano. La Russia sovietica cambiò nel febbraio 1918, la Grecia nel 1923, e la Chiesa russa mai. Dopo il 2100 lo scarto salirà a 14 giorni.","es":"La revolución rusa tuvo lugar el 25 de octubre de 1917 según el calendario juliano, que era el 7 de noviembre en el gregoriano. La Rusia soviética cambió en febrero de 1918, Grecia en 1923 y la Iglesia rusa nunca lo hizo. Después de 2100 la diferencia pasará a 14 días.","pt":"A revolução russa aconteceu em 25 de outubro de 1917 no calendário juliano, que era 7 de novembro no gregoriano. A Rússia soviética mudou em fevereiro de 1918, a Grécia em 1923, e a Igreja russa nunca mudou. Depois de 2100 a diferença passa a 14 dias.","ru":"Революция в России произошла 25 октября 1917 года по юлианскому календарю — по григорианскому это было 7 ноября. Советская Россия перешла на новый календарь в феврале 1918 года, Греция — в 1923-м, а Русская церковь так и не перешла. После 2100 года разница вырастет до 14 дней.","uk":"Революція в Росії відбулася 25 жовтня 1917 року за юліанським календарем — за григоріанським це було 7 листопада. Радянська Росія перейшла на новий календар у лютому 1918 року, Греція — 1923-го, а Російська церква так і не перейшла. Після 2100 року різниця зросте до 14 днів.","ar":"وقعت الثورة الروسية في 25 أكتوبر 1917 بحسب التقويم اليولياني، وهو ما يوافق 7 نوفمبر في التقويم الغريغوري. انتقلت روسيا السوفيتية إلى التقويم الجديد في فبراير 1918، واليونان في 1923، أما الكنيسة الروسية فلم تنتقل قط. وبعد عام 2100 سيتسع الفارق إلى 14 يومًا.","he":"המהפכה ברוסיה התרחשה ב־25 באוקטובר 1917 לפי הלוח היוליאני, שהוא 7 בנובמבר בלוח הגרגוריאני. רוסיה הסובייטית עברה ללוח החדש בפברואר 1918, יוון ב־1923, והכנסייה הרוסית מעולם לא עברה. אחרי 2100 יגדל הפער ל־14 ימים.","sw":"Mapinduzi ya Urusi yalitokea tarehe 25 Oktoba 1917 kwa kalenda ya Juliasi, yaani tarehe 7 Novemba kwa kalenda ya Gregori. Urusi ya Kisovieti ilibadilisha Februari 1918, Ugiriki mwaka 1923, na Kanisa la Urusi halikubadilisha kamwe. Baada ya 2100 tofauti itakuwa siku 14."},"body":{"en":"<p>The Bolsheviks took power in Petrograd on <strong>25 October 1917</strong>. That date is in the Julian calendar, which Russia still used. In the Gregorian calendar used across most of Europe the same day was <strong>7 November</strong>, and the Soviet Union held its anniversary parades on Red Square on 7 November. The revolution that brought down the tsar earlier that year also has two dates. The strikes and women's marches in Petrograd began on 23 February, which was 8 March in the Gregorian calendar, International Women's Day.</p><h3>Where the thirteen days came from</h3><p>The Julian calendar came into force in 45 BCE. It adds a leap day every fourth year, so its year averages 365.25 days, about 11 minutes longer than the solar year. In 1582 Pope Gregory XIII's reform dropped ten days and kept century years as leap years only if they divide by 400. The years 1700, 1800 and 1900 were leap years in the Julian calendar but not in the Gregorian, so the gap grew from 10 days to 11, then 12, and from March 1900 to 13.</p><h3>The decree of January 1918</h3><p>Russia had counted years from the birth of Christ only since 1 January 1700. Before that, Peter the Great's Russia counted from the creation of the world, and the year then under way was 7208. The months and days stayed Julian. On 24 January 1918 (Old Style), the Council of People's Commissars decreed that the day after 31 January would be called 14 February instead of 1 February. Deadlines of obligations under contract or law that fell between 1 and 14 February moved 13 days later. Until 1 July 1918, documents had to give the old date in brackets after the new one. On the map, Gregorian 14 February 1918 has the Julian label <em>1 февраля 1918 г. (ст. ст.)</em>, or \"1 February 1918 (Old Style)\". That is what Russia would have called the day under the old calendar.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1917-11-07\" data-cal=\"julian\">📅 7 November 1917 in the Julian calendar</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1918-02-14\" data-cal=\"julian\">📅 14 February 1918: Russia's first New Style day</button></div><h3>The church kept the Old Style</h3><p>The Russian Orthodox Church did not change. Patriarch Tikhon ordered the new style in October 1923, but he withdrew the order within weeks when clergy and parishes resisted. The church still dates its fixed feasts by the Julian calendar. Christmas is 25 December Old Style, which is 7 January Gregorian. The <em>Stary Novy God</em> (Old New Year) on the night of 13–14 January is the Julian 1 January. The Serbian, Georgian and Jerusalem churches and the monasteries of Mount Athos keep the same calendar. The Orthodox Church of Ukraine left it on 1 September 2023 and now celebrates Christmas on 25 December.</p><h3>Greece, 1923</h3><p>Greece was the last state in Europe to change its civil calendar. There, 15 February 1923 was followed by 1 March 1923. In March 1924 the Church of Greece adopted the Revised Julian calendar, which Milutin Milanković had proposed at the 1923 congress in Constantinople. Its fixed dates match the Gregorian calendar until 2800. The Greek and Russian churches still calculate Easter by the Julian calendar.</p><h3>Fourteen days after 2100</h3><p>The gap will not stay at 13 days. 2100 is a leap year in the Julian calendar but not in the Gregorian. Julian 29 February 2100 falls on Gregorian 14 March 2100, and from then on the difference is 14 days. Christmas of 2100 Old Style will fall on 8 January 2101. In 2200 the gap becomes 15 days and in 2300 it becomes 16. It stays at 16 through 2400, which is a leap year in both calendars.</p>"},"sources":[{"text":"Council of People's Commissars (Sovnarkom), 24 January (6 February) 1918, Декрет о введении в Российской республике западноевропейского календаря, in Декреты Советской власти, vol. 1 (Moscow, 1957); e-text at Moscow State University History Faculty","url":"http://www.hist.msu.ru/ER/Etext/DEKRET/18-01-24.htm"},{"text":"Lewis Siegelbaum, Seventeen Moments in Soviet History (Michigan State University), \"The New Calendar and Alphabet Reform\"","url":"https://soviethistory.msu.edu/1917/new-letters-and-dates/"},{"text":"Wikipedia, \"List of adoption dates of the Gregorian calendar by country\" (Greece: last Julian day 15 Feb, first Gregorian day 1 Mar 1923; Russia: 31 Jan → 14 Feb 1918)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_adoption_dates_of_the_Gregorian_calendar_by_country"},{"text":"The Kyiv Independent, 24 May 2023, \"Orthodox Church of Ukraine to switch to Revised Julian calendar, celebrate Christmas on Dec. 25\"","url":"https://kyivindependent.com/orthodox-church-of-ukraine-to-switch-to-revised-julian-calendar-celebrate-christmas-on-dec-25/"}]},{"id":"islamic-lunar-year","icon":"🌙","tags":["calendar","islam","lunar calendar","saudi arabia","iran"],"title":{"en":"The Hijri Year: 354 Days and a Moving Ramadan","ja":"ヒジュラ暦：354日の一年と移動するラマダーン","ko":"히즈라력의 1년: 354일, 그리고 움직이는 라마단","zh":"希吉拉历的一年：354天与游移的斋月","yue":"希吉拉曆一年：354日，齋月年年走位","vi":"Năm Hijri: 354 ngày và tháng Ramadan di động","th":"ปีฮิจเราะห์: 354 วันกับรอมฎอนที่เลื่อนไปเรื่อย ๆ","id":"Tahun Hijriah: 354 Hari dan Ramadan yang Berpindah-pindah","hi":"हिजरी वर्ष: 354 दिन और खिसकता रमज़ान","de":"Das Hidschra-Jahr: 354 Tage und ein wandernder Ramadan","fr":"L'année de l'Hégire : 354 jours et un ramadan qui se déplace","it":"L'anno dell'Egira: 354 giorni e un Ramadan che si sposta","es":"El año de la Hégira: 354 días y un Ramadán que se desplaza","pt":"O ano da Hégira: 354 dias e um Ramadã que se desloca","ru":"Год хиджры: 354 дня и кочующий Рамадан","uk":"Рік хіджри: 354 дні й мандрівний Рамадан","ar":"السنة الهجرية: 354 يومًا ورمضان متنقّل","he":"השנה ההיג'רית: 354 ימים ורמדאן נודד","sw":"Mwaka wa Hijria: Siku 354 na Ramadhani Inayohama"},"summary":{"en":"The Islamic calendar has twelve lunar months and no leap month, so Ramadan comes about 11 days earlier every Western year. Some communities start each month when the crescent is sighted, Saudi Arabia computes its months in advance, and the Dawoodi Bohras use a fixed table inherited from the Fatimids.","ja":"イスラームの暦は月の満ち欠けによる12か月だけで、閏月がない。そのためラマダーンは西暦の上で毎年約11日ずつ早まる。新月を目で確かめて月を始める共同体もあれば、サウジアラビアのように前もって計算する国もあり、ダーウーディー・ボーホラー派はファーティマ朝から受け継いだ固定の暦表を使う。","ko":"이슬람력은 태음월 열두 달로 이루어지고 윤달이 없어서, 라마단이 양력으로 해마다 약 11일씩 앞당겨진다. 초승달이 보이는 날에 달을 시작하는 공동체가 있는가 하면, 사우디아라비아는 달을 미리 계산해 두고, 다우디 보흐라는 파티마 왕조에서 물려받은 고정 표를 쓴다.","zh":"伊斯兰历有十二个太阴月，不设闰月，因此斋月在公历中每年提前约11天。有的社群看到新月才开始一个月，沙特阿拉伯预先推算月份，达乌迪·博赫拉派则沿用承袭自法蒂玛王朝的固定历表。","yue":"伊斯蘭曆有十二個太陰月，冇閏月，所以齋月喺西曆度每年早大約11日。有啲社群要見到新月先開始一個月，沙特阿拉伯就預先計好每個月，而達烏迪·博赫拉派就用一個由法蒂瑪王朝傳落嚟嘅固定曆表。","vi":"Lịch Hồi giáo có mười hai tháng âm lịch và không có tháng nhuận, nên mỗi năm dương lịch Ramadan lại đến sớm hơn khoảng 11 ngày. Có cộng đồng bắt đầu mỗi tháng khi nhìn thấy trăng lưỡi liềm, Ả Rập Xê Út tính trước các tháng, còn người Dawoodi Bohra dùng một bảng lịch cố định thừa hưởng từ nhà Fatimid.","th":"ปฏิทินอิสลามมีเดือนจันทรคติสิบสองเดือนและไม่มีเดือนอธิกมาส รอมฎอนจึงมาเร็วขึ้นราว 11 วันทุกปีตามปฏิทินสากล บางชุมชนเริ่มเดือนใหม่เมื่อเห็นจันทร์เสี้ยว ซาอุดีอาระเบียคำนวณเดือนไว้ล่วงหน้า ส่วนชาวดาวูดี โบห์ราใช้ตารางคงที่ที่สืบทอดมาจากราชวงศ์ฟาฏิมียะฮ์","id":"Kalender Islam memiliki dua belas bulan kamariah tanpa bulan kabisat, sehingga Ramadan datang sekitar 11 hari lebih awal setiap tahun Masehi. Sebagian komunitas memulai setiap bulan saat hilal terlihat, Arab Saudi menghitung bulan-bulannya jauh hari sebelumnya, dan kaum Dawoodi Bohra memakai tabel tetap warisan Dinasti Fatimiyah.","hi":"इस्लामी कैलेंडर में बारह चांद्र महीने होते हैं और कोई अधिक मास नहीं होता, इसलिए रमज़ान हर ईसवी वर्ष में लगभग 11 दिन पहले आ जाता है। कुछ समुदाय हर महीना नया चाँद दिखने पर शुरू करते हैं, सऊदी अरब अपने महीनों की गणना पहले से कर लेता है, और दाऊदी बोहरा फ़ातिमियों से विरासत में मिली एक स्थिर तालिका का उपयोग करते हैं।","de":"Der islamische Kalender hat zwölf Mondmonate und keinen Schaltmonat, deshalb beginnt der Ramadan in jedem westlichen Jahr etwa 11 Tage früher. Manche Gemeinschaften beginnen jeden Monat mit der Sichtung der Mondsichel, Saudi-Arabien berechnet seine Monate im Voraus, und die Dawoodi Bohras nutzen eine feste Tabelle, die sie von den Fatimiden geerbt haben.","fr":"Le calendrier islamique compte douze mois lunaires et aucun mois intercalaire : le ramadan arrive donc environ 11 jours plus tôt chaque année occidentale. Certaines communautés font commencer chaque mois à l'observation du croissant, l'Arabie saoudite calcule ses mois à l'avance, et les Dawoodi Bohras suivent une table fixe héritée des Fatimides.","it":"Il calendario islamico ha dodici mesi lunari e nessun mese intercalare, così il Ramadan arriva circa 11 giorni prima ogni anno occidentale. Alcune comunità iniziano ogni mese quando si avvista la falce di luna, l'Arabia Saudita calcola i suoi mesi in anticipo e i Dawoodi Bohra usano una tavola fissa ereditata dai Fatimidi.","es":"El calendario islámico tiene doce meses lunares y ningún mes intercalar, así que el Ramadán llega unos 11 días antes cada año occidental. Algunas comunidades empiezan cada mes cuando se avista el creciente lunar, Arabia Saudí calcula sus meses por adelantado y los bohras dawoodi usan una tabla fija heredada de los fatimíes.","pt":"O calendário islâmico tem doze meses lunares e nenhum mês intercalar, por isso o Ramadã chega cerca de 11 dias mais cedo a cada ano ocidental. Algumas comunidades iniciam cada mês quando o crescente é avistado, a Arábia Saudita calcula seus meses com antecedência e os bohras dawoodi usam uma tabela fixa herdada dos fatímidas.","ru":"В исламском календаре двенадцать лунных месяцев и нет вставного месяца, поэтому Рамадан с каждым годом по западному календарю наступает примерно на 11 дней раньше. Одни общины начинают каждый месяц, когда увидят серп молодой луны, Саудовская Аравия рассчитывает свои месяцы заранее, а дауди-бохра пользуются неизменной таблицей, унаследованной от Фатимидов.","uk":"Ісламський календар має дванадцять місячних місяців і жодного вставного, тож Рамадан щороку за західним календарем настає приблизно на 11 днів раніше. Одні громади починають кожен місяць, коли побачать молодик, Саудівська Аравія обчислює свої місяці заздалегідь, а дауді-бохра користуються незмінною таблицею, успадкованою від Фатімідів.","ar":"للتقويم الإسلامي اثنا عشر شهرًا قمريًا بلا شهر كبيس، ولذلك يأتي رمضان في كل سنة ميلادية أبكر بنحو 11 يومًا. بعض المجتمعات تبدأ كل شهر برؤية الهلال، والسعودية تحسب شهورها مسبقًا، والبهرة الداوودية تتبع جدولًا ثابتًا ورثته عن الفاطميين.","he":"ללוח השנה המוסלמי שנים-עשר חודשי ירח ואין בו חודש מעובר, ולכן רמדאן מקדים בכ-11 יום בכל שנה לועזית. יש קהילות שפותחות כל חודש כשהסהר נראה, ערב הסעודית מחשבת את חודשיה מראש, והבוהרה הדאוודים משתמשים בטבלה קבועה שירשו מהפאטמים.","sw":"Kalenda ya Kiislamu ina miezi kumi na miwili ya mwandamo na haina mwezi wa nyongeza, kwa hiyo Ramadhani huja takriban siku 11 mapema kila mwaka wa Kimagharibi. Baadhi ya jamii huanza kila mwezi pale mwezi mchanga unapoonekana, Saudi Arabia hukokotoa miezi yake mapema, na Dawoodi Bohra hutumia jedwali lisilobadilika walilorithi kutoka kwa Wafatimi."},"body":{"en":"<h3>Twelve moons and no leap month</h3><p>The Islamic, or Hijri, calendar has twelve lunar months of 29 or 30 days, from Muḥarram to Dhū al-Ḥijja. Twelve lunations come to about 354.37 days, so a Hijri year is 354 or 355 days long, about 11 days shorter than the solar year. Qur'an 9:36 sets the year at twelve months, and 9:37 condemns the <em>nasīʾ</em>, a pre-Islamic Arabian practice whose exact form is disputed. It was either the insertion of an extra month to keep the year in line with the seasons, or the postponement of a sacred month. Either way, the Hijri calendar has no thirteenth month, which is the device that keeps the Hebrew and Chinese lunisolar calendars in step with the sun.</p><h3>Ramadan moves</h3><p>Because the year is short, every Hijri date slides about 11 days earlier through the Gregorian year. In Saudi Arabia's Umm al-Qura table, 1 Ramadan 1446 fell on 1 March 2025 and 1 Ramadan 1447 on 18 February 2026, and both times the announced start of the fast agreed with it. Thirteen years earlier the table put 1 Ramadan 1434 on 9 July 2013. The crescent was not seen that evening, so Saudi Arabia began the fast on 10 July, in the longest days of the northern summer. The table's 1 Ramadan 1413 was 22 February 1993, almost exactly 33 years before the 2026 date. In those 33 Gregorian years, 34 Hijri years went by.</p><h3>Year 1 begins before the journey</h3><p>The era counts from the Hijra, Muhammad's move from Mecca to Medina in AD 622, but year 1 does not start on the day of the journey. The count was set up under the caliph ʿUmar around 17 AH (AD 638). It starts at the beginning of the lunar year in which the Hijra took place: 1 Muḥarram AH 1, which is Friday 16 July 622 in the Julian calendar, or 19 July in the proleptic Gregorian calendar the map uses. Muhammad reached Medina about two months later, in Rabīʿ al-Awwal. Arithmetic tables also use an \"astronomical\" epoch one day earlier, Thursday 15 July.</p><h3>Seen or calculated</h3><p>Under the classical rule, a month begins when the new crescent is seen in the western sky after sunset on the 29th. If it cannot be seen, the month runs to 30 days. As a result, neighbouring countries, or two mosques in the same city, can start Ramadan on different days. Saudi Arabia's Umm al-Qura calendar is computed instead, at King Abdulaziz City for Science and Technology in Riyadh. Its rule since 1423 AH (2002) works like this: on the 29th, if the conjunction falls before sunset and the moon sets after the sun at Mecca, the next day starts a new month. R. H. van Gent calculates that on about three evenings in four, the crescent is then still invisible to the naked eye.</p><p>The table is used for civil purposes. For Ramadan, Shawwāl and Dhū al-Ḥijja, and in some years Muḥarram, the authorities act on reported sightings. In 1427 AH the table put 1 Ramadan on 24 September 2006, but the announced date was 23 September. When an announcement leaves a month with 31 days, one day is counted twice: 28 and 29 December 2007 were both 19 Dhū al-Ḥijja 1428. The map follows the published table, not these announcements.</p><h3>The Bohra table</h3><p>The Dawoodi Bohras are a Shiʿi Ismaʿili community, estimated at one to one and a half million people, with their largest centres in Gujarat and Mumbai. They use a fixed arithmetic calendar inherited from the Fatimid caliphs of Egypt. Odd-numbered months have 30 days and even-numbered months 29. In 11 years of every 30 (years 2, 5, 8, 10, 13, 16, 19, 21, 24, 27 and 29 of the cycle), Dhū al-Ḥijja gets a 30th day. The cycle is 10,631 days long, which gives a mean month of 29.53056 days, against the astronomical mean of 29.53059. Because the table does not wait for the crescent, Bohra festivals can come before everyone else's. The Bohras celebrated Eid al-Fitr 1445 on 9 April 2024, Saudi Arabia on 10 April, and most of India on 11 April. On 18 February 2026 the map shows ٢ رمضان ١٤٤٧ هـ for the Bohras and ١ رمضان ١٤٤٧ هـ in Saudi Arabia.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2026-02-18\" data-cal=\"islamic\">📅 18 February 2026: 1 Ramadan 1447</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"islamic\">🗓️ The Saudi Umm al-Qura calendar</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"bohra\">🗓️ The Dawoodi Bohra calendar</button></div><h3>Iran's solar Hijri</h3><p>Iran counts from the same Hijra but in solar years. A law of 31 March 1925 (11 Farvardin 1304) made the solar Hijri calendar official. It has twelve months with Persian names, and its year begins on the day of the March equinox, or on the next day if the equinox comes after noon in Tehran. Since a solar year is about 11 days longer than a lunar one, the two counts are now 43 years apart: on 29 October 2026 the map shows ۷ آبان ۱۴۰۵ in Iran and ١٨ جمادى الأولى ١٤٤٨ هـ in Saudi Arabia. For Ramadan, Muḥarram and the other religious dates, Iran still uses the lunar Hijri calendar.</p>"},"sources":[{"text":"R. H. van Gent, \"The Umm al-Qura Calendar of Saudi Arabia\", Utrecht University (sub-pages 'astronomical rules': rules by period, KACST computation, crescent invisible on the first evening in about 75% of cases; 'Adjustment of the Umm al-Qura calendar': 1 Ramadan 1427 announced 23 Sep 2006 vs table 24 Sep, 1 Ramadan 1434 announced 10 Jul 2013 vs table 9 Jul, Muharram adjustments, 19 Dhu al-Hijja 1428 counted twice on 28-29 Dec 2007)","url":"https://webspace.science.uu.nl/~gent0113/islam/ummalqura.htm"},{"text":"Edward M. Reingold and Nachum Dershowitz, Calendrical Calculations: The Ultimate Edition, Cambridge University Press, 2018 (arithmetic Islamic calendar, epochs, Umm al-Qura, astronomical Persian calendar)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/9781107415058"},{"text":"Nagpur Today, \"Dawoodi Bohra community in Nagpur marks Eid-ul-Fitr with joyous celebrations\", 10 April 2024","url":"https://www.nagpurtoday.in/dawoodi-bohra-community-in-nagpur-marks-eid-ul-fitr-with-joyous-celebrations-service/"},{"text":"Encyclopaedia Iranica, \"Calendars\" (solar Hijri calendar adopted by the Majles, 11 Farvardin 1304 / 31 March 1925)","url":"https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/calendars"}]},{"id":"hebrew-leap-month","icon":"🕎","tags":["hebrew-calendar","lunisolar","leap-years","numerals","jewish-history"],"title":{"en":"Adar Twice: The Hebrew Calendar's Leap Month","ja":"アダル月が二度ある年：ヘブライ暦の閏月","ko":"아다르가 두 번: 히브리력의 윤달","zh":"两个亚达月：希伯来历的闰月","yue":"兩個亞達月：希伯來曆嘅閏月","vi":"Hai tháng Adar: tháng nhuận của lịch Do Thái","th":"อาดาร์สองหน: เดือนอธิกมาสของปฏิทินฮีบรู","id":"Adar Dua Kali: Bulan Kabisat Kalender Ibrani","hi":"दो बार अदार: हिब्रू कैलेंडर का अधिमास","de":"Zweimal Adar: Der Schaltmonat des hebräischen Kalenders","fr":"Deux fois Adar : le mois embolismique du calendrier hébraïque","it":"Due volte Adar: il mese embolismico del calendario ebraico","es":"Dos veces Adar: el mes intercalar del calendario hebreo","pt":"Adar duas vezes: o mês intercalar do calendário hebraico","ru":"Дважды адар: високосный месяц еврейского календаря","uk":"Двічі адар: високосний місяць єврейського календаря","ar":"أدار مرتين: الشهر الكبيس في التقويم العبري","he":"אדר פעמיים: חודש העיבור בלוח העברי","sw":"Adari Mara Mbili: Mwezi wa Ziada wa Kalenda ya Kiebrania"},"summary":{"en":"Seven years in every nineteen, the Hebrew calendar adds a second Adar to keep Passover in spring, and fixed rules stop the new year from ever falling on a Sunday, Wednesday or Friday.","ja":"ヘブライ暦は19年に7回アダル月をもう一つ加えて、過越祭を春にとどめる。新年がけっして日曜・水曜・金曜に来ないように、日をずらす規則も決まっている。","ko":"히브리력은 19년마다 7번 두 번째 아다르월을 넣어 유월절을 봄에 묶어 두고, 고정된 규칙에 따라 새해가 일요일·수요일·금요일에 오는 일은 결코 없다.","zh":"希伯来历每19年中有7年加一个第二亚达月，好让逾越节留在春天；固定的规则还让新年永远不会落在星期日、星期三或星期五。","yue":"希伯來曆每19年就有7年加多一個第二亞達月，等逾越節留喺春天；固定規則仲令新年永遠唔會落喺星期日、星期三或者星期五。","vi":"Cứ 19 năm thì có 7 năm lịch Do Thái thêm một tháng Adar thứ hai để giữ Lễ Vượt Qua ở mùa xuân, và các quy tắc cố định khiến năm mới không bao giờ rơi vào Chủ nhật, thứ Tư hay thứ Sáu.","th":"ในทุก 19 ปี ปฏิทินฮีบรูจะเพิ่มเดือนอาดาร์ที่สองเข้าไป 7 ปี เพื่อให้เทศกาลปัสกาอยู่ในฤดูใบไม้ผลิ และกฎตายตัวทำให้วันขึ้นปีใหม่ไม่มีวันตรงกับวันอาทิตย์ วันพุธ หรือวันศุกร์","id":"Dalam tujuh dari setiap sembilan belas tahun, kalender Ibrani menambahkan Adar kedua agar Pesakh tetap jatuh di musim semi, dan aturan tetap mencegah tahun baru jatuh pada hari Minggu, Rabu, atau Jumat.","hi":"हर उन्नीस में से सात वर्षों में हिब्रू कैलेंडर एक दूसरा अदार जोड़ता है ताकि पासओवर वसंत में ही पड़े, और तय नियम नव वर्ष को कभी रविवार, बुधवार या शुक्रवार को नहीं पड़ने देते।","de":"In sieben von neunzehn Jahren fügt der hebräische Kalender einen zweiten Adar ein, damit Pessach im Frühling bleibt, und feste Regeln sorgen dafür, dass das Neujahr nie auf einen Sonntag, Mittwoch oder Freitag fällt.","fr":"Sept années sur dix-neuf, le calendrier hébraïque ajoute un second Adar pour que Pessa'h reste au printemps, et des règles fixes empêchent le nouvel an de tomber un dimanche, un mercredi ou un vendredi.","it":"In sette anni su diciannove il calendario ebraico aggiunge un secondo Adar per mantenere Pesach in primavera, e regole fisse impediscono che il capodanno cada mai di domenica, mercoledì o venerdì.","es":"Siete de cada diecinueve años, el calendario hebreo añade un segundo Adar para que Pésaj siga cayendo en primavera, y unas reglas fijas impiden que el año nuevo caiga nunca en domingo, miércoles o viernes.","pt":"Em sete de cada dezenove anos, o calendário hebraico acrescenta um segundo Adar para manter o Pessach na primavera, e regras fixas impedem que o ano-novo caia num domingo, numa quarta-feira ou numa sexta-feira.","ru":"В семь лет из каждых девятнадцати еврейский календарь добавляет второй адар, чтобы Песах оставался весной, а жёсткие правила не дают Новому году выпасть на воскресенье, среду или пятницу.","uk":"У сім років із кожних дев'ятнадцяти єврейський календар додає другий адар, щоб Песах залишався навесні, а сталі правила не дають Новому року припасти на неділю, середу чи п'ятницю.","ar":"في سبع سنوات من كل تسع عشرة سنة يضيف التقويم العبري شهر أدار ثانيًا ليبقى عيد الفصح في الربيع، وتمنع قواعد ثابتة أن يقع رأس السنة يوم أحد أو أربعاء أو جمعة.","he":"בשבע שנים מתוך כל תשע־עשרה מוסיף הלוח העברי אדר שני כדי שפסח יחול באביב, וכללים קבועים מונעים מראש השנה לחול אי־פעם ביום ראשון, רביעי או שישי.","sw":"Katika miaka saba kati ya kila kumi na tisa, kalenda ya Kiebrania huongeza Adari wa pili ili Pasaka ibaki katika majira ya kuchipua, na kanuni maalum huzuia mwaka mpya usiangukie kamwe Jumapili, Jumatano au Ijumaa."},"body":{"en":"<h3>Twelve moons fall eleven days short</h3><p>Twelve lunar months of 29 or 30 days come to about 354 days, eleven short of the solar year. The Islamic calendar accepts the shortfall, and its festivals pass through every season in about 33 years. The Hebrew calendar cannot do that. Passover falls on 15 Nisan, and Deuteronomy 16:1 ties it to the month of <em>aviv</em>, the ripening spring barley. So in 7 years out of every 19 the calendar inserts a thirteenth month. Nineteen solar years come to about 6,939.60 days, and 235 lunar months (19 × 12 + 7) to about 6,939.69, so the calendar slips later against the seasons by about one day every 216 years. The leap years are years 3, 6, 8, 11, 14, 17 and 19 of each cycle.</p><h3>Which Adar is the extra one</h3><p>The extra month goes in before Adar, the month before Nisan. A leap year has <strong>Adar I</strong> (אדר א׳, 30 days) followed by <strong>Adar II</strong> (אדר ב׳, 29 days). Adar II counts as the ordinary Adar, so Purim is kept on 14 Adar II. The year 5787, which began on 12 September 2026, is year 11 of its cycle. On the map, 1 Adar I 5787 falls on 8 February 2027, 1 Adar II on 10 March, Purim on 23 March and Passover on 22 April. Hebrew days begin at sunset, so each of these festivals starts on the evening before the date the map shows. A common year has 353, 354 or 355 days and a leap year 383, 384 or 385. The year 5786 had 354 days, and 5787 has 385.</p><h3>A new year in the seventh month</h3><p>Exodus 12:2 makes Nisan, the spring month, the first of the months, and months are still numbered from it, so Tishri is the seventh. But the year number changes on 1 Tishri, Rosh Hashanah, in September or October. The Mishnah (Rosh Hashanah 1:1) lists four new years:</p><ul><li>1 Nisan, for kings and festivals</li><li>1 Elul, for the tithe of cattle</li><li>1 Tishri, for years, sabbatical years and jubilees</li><li>1 or 15 Shevat, for trees (the schools of Shammai and Hillel disagree on which day)</li></ul><p>Years are counted <em>Anno Mundi</em>, from a date for Creation that the calculation places in the autumn of 3761 BCE.</p><h3>Writing the year in letters</h3><p>The map writes dates in Hebrew letter-numerals. Rosh Hashanah 5787 appears as <strong>א׳ בתשרי תשפ״ז</strong>, 1 Tishri 5787. In the year number ת = 400, ש = 300, פ = 80 and ז = 7, which makes 787. The thousands are left out; the full form ה׳תשפ״ז adds ה = 5. The double stroke ״ (<em>gershayim</em>) goes before the last letter. Fifteen is written ט״ו (9 + 6) rather than י״ה (10 + 5), because those two letters spell a name of God, and 16 is written ט״ז for the same reason. Passover 5787 therefore shows on the map as ט״ו בניסן תשפ״ז.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"hebrew\">🗓️ Show the Hebrew calendar on the map</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2026-09-12\" data-cal=\"hebrew\">📅 Rosh Hashanah 5787 (12 September 2026)</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2027-03-10\" data-cal=\"hebrew\">📅 1 Adar II 5787 (10 March 2027)</button></div><h3>From sighting to calculation</h3><p>New months were once proclaimed by a court on the testimony of witnesses who had seen the new crescent, and leap years were added by decision. Hai Gaon (died 1038) is the first to record the tradition that Hillel II introduced the calculated calendar in the year 670 of the Seleucid era, 358/359 CE. Historians date the rules later and in stages. The Rosh Hashanah rules took their modern form between about 629 and 648. The fixed 19-year cycle probably dates from the late 8th century. Al-Khwarizmi described the system largely in its present form in 823. In 921 Aaron ben Meir in Palestine ruled that Tishri should begin on the day of the calculated new moon unless it came more than 642 parts after noon. The Babylonian academies, with Saadia Gaon among their spokesmen, kept noon as the cut-off. In 922 the two communities kept Passover two days apart. Maimonides set out the complete rules in his <em>Mishneh Torah</em> in 1178.</p><h3>Days the new year cannot fall on</h3><p>The calculation starts from the <em>molad</em>, the mean new moon, which recurs every 29 days 12 hours and 793 parts; an hour has 1,080 parts. If the molad of Tishri comes at or after noon, Rosh Hashanah moves to the next day. It also never falls on a Sunday, Wednesday or Friday. The rule is called <em>lo ADU rosh</em>, from the letters א, ד and ו, which stand for days 1, 4 and 6 of the week. If the year began on a Wednesday or a Friday, Yom Kippur (10 Tishri) would fall on the day just before or after the Sabbath. If it began on a Sunday, Hoshana Rabbah (21 Tishri), with its willow-beating rite, would fall on the Sabbath. Two rarer rules keep each year within the permitted lengths. On the map, 1 Tishri falls on a Monday 56 times between 1900 and 2100, on a Tuesday 23 times, on a Thursday 63 times and on a Saturday 59 times. It never falls on any other day.</p>"},"sources":[{"text":"Sacha Stern (2001). Calendar and Community: A History of the Jewish Calendar, Second Century BCE – Tenth Century CE. Oxford University Press.","url":"https://global.oup.com/academic/product/calendar-and-community-9780198270348"},{"text":"Sacha Stern (2019). The Jewish Calendar Controversy of 921/2 CE. Time, Astronomy, and Calendars 7. Leiden: Brill.","url":"https://collaborate.princeton.edu/en/publications/the-jewish-calendar-controversy-of-921-22-reconstructing-the-manu/"},{"text":"Edward M. Reingold & Nachum Dershowitz (2018). Calendrical Calculations: The Ultimate Edition, ch. 8 'The Hebrew Calendar', pp. 113–142. Cambridge University Press.","url":"https://resolve.cambridge.org/core/books/calendrical-calculations/hebrew-calendar/29140DA5B275CB2AB3443992E9BBB115"},{"text":"Hebrew calendar (Wikipedia): leap cycle, molad, dehiyyot, Hai Gaon on Hillel II, staged fixation 629–823, drift of one day in about 216 years","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hebrew_calendar"}]},{"id":"japanese-era-names","icon":"🎌","tags":["japan","era-names","calendars","imperial-history"],"title":{"en":"Japanese Era Names: From Taika to Reiwa","ja":"元号：大化から令和まで","ko":"일본의 연호: 다이카에서 레이와까지","zh":"日本年号：从大化到令和","yue":"日本年號：由大化到令和","vi":"Niên hiệu Nhật Bản: Từ Taika đến Reiwa","th":"ศักราชญี่ปุ่น: จากไทกะถึงเรวะ","id":"Nama Era Jepang: Dari Taika hingga Reiwa","hi":"जापानी युग-नाम: ताइका से रेइवा तक","de":"Japanische Ära-Namen: Von Taika bis Reiwa","fr":"Les noms d'ère japonais : de Taika à Reiwa","it":"I nomi di era giapponesi: da Taika a Reiwa","es":"Los nombres de era japoneses: de Taika a Reiwa","pt":"Os nomes de era japoneses: de Taika a Reiwa","ru":"Японские девизы правления: от Тайка до Рэйва","uk":"Японські девізи правління: від Тайка до Рейва","ar":"أسماء العهود اليابانية: من تايكا إلى ريوا","he":"שמות התקופה היפניים: מטאיקה ועד רייווה","sw":"Majina ya Enzi ya Japani: Kutoka Taika hadi Reiwa"},"summary":{"en":"Japan has counted years by era name since Taika in 645. Since 1868 each reign has had a single era, and the 1979 Era Name Law allows a change only when a new emperor succeeds.","ja":"日本では645年の大化以来、元号で年を数えてきた。1868年からは天皇一代に元号一つとなり、1979年の元号法で改元は皇位継承のときに限ると定められた。","ko":"일본은 645년 다이카 이래 연호로 해를 세어 왔다. 1868년부터는 천황 한 대에 연호 하나만 쓰며, 1979년 원호법은 새 천황이 즉위할 때에만 연호를 바꿀 수 있도록 정하고 있다.","zh":"日本自645年的大化起以年号纪年。1868年以后，每位天皇在位期间只用一个年号；1979年的《元号法》规定，只有在新天皇即位时才能改元。","yue":"日本由645年嘅大化開始用年號紀年。1868年起每位天皇在位期間只用一個年號，而1979年嘅《元號法》規定，只有新天皇即位先可以改元。","vi":"Nhật Bản tính năm theo niên hiệu kể từ niên hiệu Taika năm 645. Từ năm 1868, mỗi triều chỉ có một niên hiệu, và Luật Niên hiệu năm 1979 chỉ cho phép đổi niên hiệu khi có thiên hoàng mới kế vị.","th":"ญี่ปุ่นนับปีตามชื่อศักราชมาตั้งแต่ศักราชไทกะในปี 645 นับแต่ปี 1868 จักรพรรดิแต่ละรัชกาลมีศักราชเดียว และกฎหมายว่าด้วยชื่อศักราชปี 1979 อนุญาตให้เปลี่ยนศักราชได้เฉพาะเมื่อมีจักรพรรดิองค์ใหม่สืบราชสมบัติเท่านั้น","id":"Jepang menghitung tahun berdasarkan nama era sejak Taika pada 645. Sejak 1868 setiap masa pemerintahan hanya memiliki satu era, dan Undang-Undang Nama Era 1979 hanya mengizinkan pergantian ketika kaisar baru naik takhta.","hi":"जापान में 645 के ताइका युग से वर्षों की गिनती युग-नामों से होती आई है। 1868 से हर शासनकाल का एक ही युग रहा है, और 1979 का युग-नाम क़ानून युग बदलने की अनुमति केवल तभी देता है जब नया सम्राट गद्दी पर बैठे।","de":"Japan zählt die Jahre seit Taika im Jahr 645 nach Ära-Namen. Seit 1868 hat jede Regierungszeit nur eine einzige Ära, und das Ära-Namen-Gesetz von 1979 erlaubt einen Wechsel nur bei der Thronfolge eines neuen Kaisers.","fr":"Le Japon compte les années par noms d'ère depuis Taika, en 645. Depuis 1868, chaque règne n'a qu'une seule ère, et la loi sur les noms d'ère de 1979 n'autorise un changement qu'à l'avènement d'un nouvel empereur.","it":"Il Giappone conta gli anni per nomi di era dal 645, anno di Taika. Dal 1868 ogni regno ha una sola era, e la Legge sui nomi di era del 1979 ne consente il cambio solo quando sale al trono un nuovo imperatore.","es":"Japón cuenta los años por nombres de era desde Taika, en 645. Desde 1868 cada reinado tiene una sola era, y la Ley de Nombres de Era de 1979 solo permite cambiarla cuando sube al trono un nuevo emperador.","pt":"O Japão conta os anos por nomes de era desde Taika, em 645. Desde 1868 cada reinado tem uma única era, e a Lei dos Nomes de Era de 1979 só permite a mudança quando um novo imperador sobe ao trono.","ru":"Японцы ведут счёт годам по девизам правления с 645 года, когда был провозглашён девиз Тайка. С 1868 года каждому царствованию соответствует один девиз, а Закон о девизах правления 1979 года допускает смену девиза только при вступлении на престол нового императора.","uk":"Японія лічить роки за девізами правління від девізу Тайка 645 року. Від 1868 року кожне царювання має лише один девіз, а Закон про девізи правління 1979 року дозволяє змінювати девіз тільки тоді, коли на престол вступає новий імператор.","ar":"تعدّ اليابان السنين بأسماء العهود منذ عهد تايكا عام 645. ومنذ عام 1868 صار لكل فترة حكم عهد واحد فقط، ولا يسمح قانون أسماء العهود الصادر عام 1979 بتغيير الاسم إلا عند تولّي إمبراطور جديد العرش.","he":"ביפן סופרים את השנים לפי שמות תקופה מאז טאיקה בשנת 645. מאז 1868 יש לכל תקופת שלטון שם תקופה אחד בלבד, וחוק שמות התקופה משנת 1979 מתיר החלפה רק כשקיסר חדש עולה לכס.","sw":"Japani imehesabu miaka kwa majina ya enzi tangu Taika mwaka 645. Tangu 1868 kila utawala umekuwa na enzi moja tu, na Sheria ya Majina ya Enzi ya 1979 inaruhusu mabadiliko pale tu mfalme mpya anaporithi kiti cha ufalme."},"body":{"en":"<h3>From Taika to Taihō</h3><p>Japan's first era name, <strong>大化</strong> <em>Taika</em> (\"great change\"), was proclaimed in 645, the year Prince Naka no Ōe and Nakatomi no Kamatari overthrew the Soga clan. For the next half-century era names were used only intermittently: 白雉 <em>Hakuchi</em> followed in 650, and long gaps came after it. The unbroken sequence starts with 大宝 <em>Taihō</em> in 701. Chief Cabinet Secretary Yoshihide Suga announced 令和 <em>Reiwa</em> on 1 April 2019; in the usual count it is the 248th era. That count includes the eras of both rival courts of the Northern and Southern Courts period (1336–1392), when each line proclaimed its own.</p><h3>Many eras per reign</h3><p>Before 1868 the court changed the era whenever it saw a reason to: an auspicious omen, an earthquake, an epidemic, or one of the two years of the sixty-year cycle that were believed to bring upheaval, 辛酉 <em>kanoto-tori</em> and 甲子 <em>kinoe-ne</em>. Emperor Kōmei (reigned 1846–1867) proclaimed six new eras between 1848 and 1865: 嘉永 <em>Kaei</em>, 安政 <em>Ansei</em> (after the earthquakes of 1854), 万延 <em>Man'en</em>, 文久 <em>Bunkyū</em> (1861, a <em>kanoto-tori</em> year), 元治 <em>Genji</em> (1864, a <em>kinoe-ne</em> year) and 慶応 <em>Keiō</em>.</p><h3>One reign, one era</h3><p>An edict dated the 8th day of the 9th month of Keiō 4 (23 October 1868) renamed the whole of Keiō 4 as Meiji 1. It also ruled that each reign would have a single era, <strong>一世一元</strong> <em>issei ichigen</em>. Article 12 of the 1889 Imperial Household Law wrote the rule into law. Since then the era also gives each emperor his posthumous name, so the Meiji Emperor is named after his era. The first year of an era is written 元年 <em>gannen</em>, not 1年. Under the Meiji rule the new era began on the day of accession: Taishō on 30 July 1912, the day the Meiji Emperor died, and Shōwa on 25 December 1926, the day Emperor Taishō died. Shōwa 64 lasted only seven days, 1–7 January 1989: Emperor Shōwa died on 7 January, and Heisei began the next day, 8 January. The map shows Japanese era dates from 1 January 1873 (Meiji 6). Japan adopted the Gregorian calendar by making the 3rd day of the 12th month of Meiji 5 into that date, and before it era years were reckoned on the lunisolar calendar.</p><h3>The 1979 law</h3><p>The postwar Imperial Household Law of 1947 dropped the clause on era names, so from 1947 Shōwa remained in use by custom alone. The <strong>Era Name Law</strong> (元号法 <em>Gengō-hō</em>, Law No. 43 of 12 June 1979) has two clauses: the era name is set by cabinet order, and it changes only when an emperor succeeds to the throne. A supplementary provision deems Shōwa to have been set under it. The law does not require private citizens to use era names. 平成 <em>Heisei</em> was the first era chosen under it, from phrases in the <em>Shiji</em> and the <em>Book of Documents</em>.</p><h3>Reiwa</h3><p>Emperor Akihito abdicated on 30 April 2019, the first succession by abdication in about two hundred years. Because the date was known in advance, the new name was announced a month early. The year 2019 therefore runs from 1 January to 30 April as Heisei 31 and from 1 May as Reiwa 1. The map shows 平成31年4月30日 and then 令和元年5月1日. The government described Reiwa as the first era name, as far as records show, taken from a Japanese book rather than a Chinese classic. Its source is the preface to the thirty-two plum-blossom poems in Book 5 of the <em>Man'yōshū</em>, which describes a banquet at Ōtomo no Tabito's residence in Dazaifu on the 13th day of the 1st month of Tenpyō 2 (730): 初春令月、氣淑風和 \"in the fine month of early spring, the air is clear and the wind is gentle\". The name comes from that prose preface, not from one of the poems. The preface is written in Chinese, and annotators trace its 令月 to \"Returning to the Fields\" by the Eastern Han poet Zhang Heng (78–139), preserved in the sixth-century <em>Wen xuan</em>, which has 仲春令月、時和氣清. Five of the eight characters are the same. On 2 April 2019 the Foreign Ministry gave \"beautiful harmony\" as the English explanation of the name, after some overseas reports had glossed 令 as \"command\"; it said this explained the meaning and was not an official translation.</p><h3>The imperial year</h3><p>Historical mode also shows <strong>皇紀</strong> <em>Kōki</em>, a count of years from the accession of the legendary first emperor Jimmu. The government adopted it in 1872, and it places that accession in 660 BC, a date taken from the chronology of the <em>Nihon Shoki</em> that has no historical basis. A Kōki year is the Western year plus 660, so 1940 was 2600. A state ceremony for the anniversary was held in front of the Imperial Palace on 10 November 1940, and the navy's Type 0 carrier fighter, adopted that year, took its \"0\" from the last digit of 2600.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2019-05-01\" data-cal=\"japanese\">📅 Go to 1 May 2019, Reiwa 1</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"koki\">🗓️ Show the imperial year (Kōki)</button></div>"},"sources":[{"text":"Cabinet Office, Government of Japan (内閣府). 元号 (Era names): Era Name Law (Law No. 43 of 1979), cabinet orders and statements on Heisei (1989) and Reiwa (2019).","url":"https://www.cao.go.jp/others/soumu/gengou/index.html"},{"text":"National Astronomical Observatory of Japan, Koyomi Calculation Office. 暦Wiki: 元号/明治 (Meiji edict of 1868, Taika 645, continuous eras from Taihō 701).","url":"https://eco.mtk.nao.ac.jp/koyomi/wiki/CEF2BBCB2FB8B5B9E6.html"},{"text":"Kaminaga Satoru (神永曉), JapanKnowledge (Shogakukan), 29 April 2019. 日本語、どうでしょう？ 第405回「新元号と『万葉集』」 (the Man'yōshū preface, the banquet of 730 at Ōtomo no Tabito's residence, and Zhang Heng's 帰田賦 in the Wen xuan).","url":"https://japanknowledge.com/articles/blognihongo/entry.html?entryid=406"},{"text":"Kenneth J. Ruoff, 2010. Imperial Japan at Its Zenith: The Wartime Celebration of the Empire's 2,600th Anniversary. Cornell University Press.","url":"https://cir.nii.ac.jp/crid/1130000796985867648?lang=en"}]},{"id":"ethiopian-13-months","icon":"☀️","tags":["calendars","ethiopia","coptic","chronology","new-year"],"title":{"en":"Thirteen Months, Seven Years Behind: The Ethiopian Calendar","ja":"エチオピア暦：13番目の月と7〜8年の差","ko":"열세 달, 7년 늦은 달력: 에티오피아력","zh":"十三个月，晚七年：埃塞俄比亚历","yue":"十三個月，遲七年：埃塞俄比亞曆","vi":"Mười ba tháng, chậm bảy năm: Lịch Ethiopia","th":"สิบสามเดือน ช้าไปเจ็ดปี: ปฏิทินเอธิโอเปีย","id":"Tiga Belas Bulan, Tertinggal Tujuh Tahun: Kalender Etiopia","hi":"तेरह महीने, सात साल पीछे: इथियोपियाई कैलेंडर","de":"Dreizehn Monate, sieben Jahre zurück: Der äthiopische Kalender","fr":"Treize mois et sept ans de retard : le calendrier éthiopien","it":"Tredici mesi e sette anni indietro: il calendario etiope","es":"Trece meses y siete años de retraso: el calendario etíope","pt":"Treze meses, sete anos atrás: o calendário etíope","ru":"Тринадцать месяцев и семь лет отставания: эфиопский календарь","uk":"Тринадцять місяців і сім років позаду: ефіопський календар","ar":"ثلاثة عشر شهرًا وتأخّر سبع سنوات: التقويم الإثيوبي","he":"שלושה־עשר חודשים, שבע שנים מאחור: הלוח האתיופי","sw":"Miezi Kumi na Mitatu, Nyuma kwa Miaka Saba: Kalenda ya Ethiopia"},"summary":{"en":"Ethiopia's calendar has twelve 30-day months plus a five- or six-day Pagume. It counts its years from an Alexandrian date for the Incarnation, and it reached the year 2000 on 12 September 2007.","ja":"エチオピア暦は30日の月12か月に、5日か6日のパグメを加えた暦である。年はアレクサンドリアで計算された受肉の年から数え、2000年を迎えたのは2007年9月12日だった。","ko":"에티오피아력은 30일짜리 열두 달에 5일 또는 6일인 파구메를 더한 달력이다. 알렉산드리아식으로 계산한 성육신 날짜를 기준으로 해를 세며, 2007년 9월 12일에 2000년을 맞았다.","zh":"埃塞俄比亚历有十二个30天的月份，外加一个五天或六天的帕古梅月。它以亚历山大里亚推算的道成肉身日期为纪年起点，并在2007年9月12日进入2000年。","yue":"埃塞俄比亞曆有十二個30日嘅月，再加一個五日或者六日嘅帕古梅月。佢以亞歷山大港推算嘅道成肉身日期做紀年起點，喺2007年9月12號踏入2000年。","vi":"Lịch Ethiopia có mười hai tháng 30 ngày cộng thêm tháng Pagume dài năm hoặc sáu ngày. Lịch này tính năm từ ngày Nhập Thể theo cách tính của Alexandria, và bước sang năm 2000 vào ngày 12 tháng 9 năm 2007.","th":"ปฏิทินเอธิโอเปียมีสิบสองเดือนเดือนละ 30 วัน บวกเดือนปากูเมอีกห้าหรือหกวัน นับปีจากวันจุติของพระคริสต์ตามการคำนวณของอะเล็กซานเดรีย และขึ้นปี 2000 เมื่อวันที่ 12 กันยายน 2007","id":"Kalender Etiopia memiliki dua belas bulan yang masing-masing 30 hari, ditambah bulan Pagume yang lamanya lima atau enam hari. Tahunnya dihitung dari tanggal Inkarnasi menurut perhitungan Aleksandria, dan kalender ini memasuki tahun 2000 pada 12 September 2007.","hi":"इथियोपिया के कैलेंडर में 30-30 दिनों के बारह महीने होते हैं और उनके बाद पाँच या छह दिनों का पागुमे। यह अपने वर्ष अवतार की एक अलेक्ज़ान्द्रियाई तिथि से गिनता है, और 12 सितंबर 2007 को वर्ष 2000 में पहुँचा।","de":"Der äthiopische Kalender hat zwölf Monate zu je 30 Tagen und dazu den fünf- oder sechstägigen Pagume. Er zählt seine Jahre ab einem alexandrinischen Datum der Menschwerdung Christi und erreichte am 12. September 2007 das Jahr 2000.","fr":"Le calendrier éthiopien compte douze mois de 30 jours, plus un mois de Pagume de cinq ou six jours. Il compte les années à partir d'une date alexandrine de l'Incarnation et a atteint l'an 2000 le 12 septembre 2007.","it":"Il calendario etiope ha dodici mesi di 30 giorni più un Pagume di cinque o sei giorni. Conta gli anni da una data alessandrina dell'Incarnazione e ha raggiunto l'anno 2000 il 12 settembre 2007.","es":"El calendario de Etiopía tiene doce meses de 30 días más un Pagume de cinco o seis días. Cuenta los años desde una fecha alejandrina de la Encarnación y llegó al año 2000 el 12 de septiembre de 2007.","pt":"O calendário da Etiópia tem doze meses de 30 dias e mais um Pagume de cinco ou seis dias. Conta os anos a partir de uma data alexandrina para a Encarnação e chegou ao ano 2000 em 12 de setembro de 2007.","ru":"В эфиопском календаре двенадцать месяцев по 30 дней и пагуме из пяти или шести дней. Годы в нём отсчитываются от александрийской даты Воплощения, а 2000 год наступил 12 сентября 2007 года.","uk":"В ефіопському календарі дванадцять місяців по 30 днів і пагуме з п’яти або шести днів. Роки в ньому відлічують від александрійської дати Втілення, а 2000 рік настав 12 вересня 2007 року.","ar":"في التقويم الإثيوبي اثنا عشر شهرًا كلٌّ منها 30 يومًا، يليها شهر باجومي ذو الأيام الخمسة أو الستة. وهو يعدّ سنواته من تاريخ سكندري للتجسّد، وقد بلغ سنة 2000 في 12 سبتمبر 2007.","he":"בלוח האתיופי שנים־עשר חודשים בני 30 יום ועוד פגומה בן חמישה או שישה ימים. הוא סופר את שנותיו מתאריך אלכסנדרוני להתגלמות, והגיע לשנת 2000 ב־12 בספטמבר 2007.","sw":"Kalenda ya Ethiopia ina miezi kumi na miwili ya siku 30 kila mmoja, pamoja na Pagume yenye siku tano au sita. Huhesabu miaka yake kuanzia tarehe ya Umwilisho kwa hesabu ya Aleksandria, na ilifikia mwaka 2000 tarehe 12 Septemba 2007."},"body":{"en":"<h3>Twelve months of thirty days, and Pagume</h3><p>The Ethiopian year has twelve months of exactly 30 days: Meskerem, Tikimt, Hidar, Tahsas, Tir, Yekatit, Megabit, Miyazya, Ginbot, Sene, Hamle and Nehase. A thirteenth month, <strong>Pagume</strong> (ጳጉሜን), follows them. It has 5 days, or 6 every fourth year. The name comes from Greek <em>epagomenai</em>, \"added (days)\", the term used in Greek-speaking Egypt for the five days left over after 360. The leap rule has no exceptions, so it is the Julian rule. 1 Meskerem always falls on 29 August in the Julian calendar, or on 30 August in the year before a Julian leap year.</p><h3>Why Enkutatash moves between 11 and 12 September</h3><p>Between 1900 and 2099 the Julian calendar runs 13 days behind the Gregorian. The Ethiopian New Year, <strong>Enkutatash</strong>, therefore lands on 11 September. It moves to 12 September when the Ethiopian year just ending had a sixth day of Pagume, which happens in the year before a Gregorian leap year. Ethiopian year 2019 is one of those: 6 Pagume 2019 is 11 September 2027, and 2020 begins on 12 September 2027. The Gregorian calendar drops the leap day in 2100 and the Ethiopian calendar does not. From September 2100 the New Year will fall on 12 September, and on 13 September in the year before a Gregorian leap year.</p><h3>Seven or eight years behind</h3><p>The gap in year numbers comes from a different date for the Incarnation. Annianus, a monk in Alexandria around 400, placed the Creation on 25 March 5492 BC and the Incarnation 5,500 years later, on 25 March AD 9. Ethiopia's <em>Amätä Məḥrät</em>, \"Year of Mercy\", is abbreviated ዓ.ም. after the year number. It counts from the Alexandrian New Year that came before that March: 29 August AD 8. Western AD numbering goes back to the Easter table that Dionysius Exiguus drew up in Rome in 525, which counted from an earlier Incarnation. The result is that from 1 Meskerem to 31 December the Ethiopian year is the Gregorian year minus 7. From 1 January to the eve of Enkutatash it is the Gregorian year minus 8. The older church count from the Creation, <em>Amätä ʿAläm</em>, is the same year number plus 5,500.</p><h3>The millennium of 2007</h3><p>Ethiopian year 1999 had six days of Pagume. The map therefore shows 11 September 2007 as <em>ጳጉሜን 6 ቀን 1999 ዓ.ም.</em> and the next day, Wednesday 12 September 2007, as <em>መስከረም 1 ቀን 2000 ዓ.ም.</em>, the first day of the year 2000. Ethiopia celebrated that day as its millennium. AFP reported on the preparations in Addis Ababa: a temporary 20,000-capacity venue that reportedly cost $10 million, and concert tickets at $270 to $330 in a country where average annual income per head had peaked at $160 in 2005. A 10 km Millennium Run organised by Haile Gebrselassie was also planned.</p><h3>The Coptic twin</h3><p>The Coptic calendar of Egypt has the same structure and the same leap rule, and its months begin on the same days. 1 Meskerem is 1 Tut, the Coptic New Year (Nayrouz). Only the era is different. The Coptic Era of the Martyrs counts from 29 August 284, the start of the first regnal year of Diocletian, who became emperor that November. That is 276 years after the Ethiopian epoch. That makes 1 Meskerem 2000 the same day as 1 Tut 1724, shown on the map as <em>١ توت ١٧٢٤ للشهداء</em>. Both calendars descend from the Egyptian civil year of 12 × 30 + 5 days. The Alexandrian reform under Augustus added the sixth day every fourth year.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2007-09-12\" data-cal=\"ethiopic\">📅 Go to 12 September 2007, the first day of Ethiopian year 2000</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"coptic\">🗓️ Show the Coptic calendar</button></div><h3>Thirteen months of sunshine</h3><p><em>13 Months of Sunshine</em> is a tourism slogan. Habteselassie Tafesse (1927–2017) headed the Ethiopian Tourism Organization from the 1960s, and The Reporter's 2017 obituary of him credits him with coining it. The thirteenth month lasts five or six days. The slogan also leaves out the main rainy season, <em>kiremt</em>, which runs across the highlands from about June to September. Pagume falls at the end of kiremt, from 6 to 10 September, or to 11 September in a leap year.</p>"},"sources":[{"text":"Dershowitz, Nachum & Reingold, Edward M. (2018). Calendrical Calculations: The Ultimate Edition, ch. 'The Coptic and Ethiopic Calendars'. Cambridge University Press.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/9781107415058"},{"text":"Mosshammer, Alden A. (2008). The Easter Computus and the Origins of the Christian Era. Oxford University Press (Annianus of Alexandria, Dionysius Exiguus).","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199543120.001.0001"},{"text":"Maasho, Aaron / AFP (2007). 'Some Ethiopians cringe at lavish millennium bash'. Mail & Guardian, 3 September 2007.","url":"https://mg.co.za/article/2007-09-03-some-ethiopians-cringe-at-lavish-millennium-bash/"},{"text":"The Reporter (Ethiopia) (2017). 'The father of tourism – Hapteselassie Tafesse', 12 August 2017.","url":"https://www.thereporterethiopia.com/252/"}]},{"id":"french-republican-calendar","icon":"🇫🇷","tags":["calendar","french revolution","france","ten-day week","napoleon"],"title":{"en":"The French Republican Calendar: Ten-Day Weeks and Days Named for Ploughs","ja":"フランス革命暦：10日の週と、犂の名を持つ日","ko":"프랑스 공화력: 열흘짜리 주와 쟁기의 이름을 딴 날","zh":"法国共和历：十天一周，以犁命名的日子","yue":"法國共和曆：十日一個禮拜，日子用犁嚟命名","vi":"Lịch Cộng hòa Pháp: tuần mười ngày và những ngày mang tên cái cày","th":"ปฏิทินสาธารณรัฐฝรั่งเศส: สัปดาห์ละสิบวัน และวันที่ตั้งชื่อตามคันไถ","id":"Kalender Republik Prancis: Pekan Sepuluh Hari dan Hari yang Dinamai Bajak","hi":"फ़्रांसीसी गणतंत्रीय कैलेंडर: दस दिन के सप्ताह और हल के नाम पर दिन","de":"Der französische Revolutionskalender: Zehntagewochen und Tage, die nach Pflügen heißen","fr":"Le calendrier républicain français : des semaines de dix jours et des jours nommés d'après la charrue","it":"Il calendario rivoluzionario francese: settimane di dieci giorni e giorni intitolati all'aratro","es":"El calendario republicano francés: semanas de diez días y días con nombre de arado","pt":"O calendário republicano francês: semanas de dez dias e dias com nome de arado","ru":"Французский республиканский календарь: десятидневные недели и дни в честь плуга","uk":"Французький республіканський календар: десятиденні тижні й дні на честь плуга","ar":"التقويم الجمهوري الفرنسي: أسابيع من عشرة أيام وأيام سُمّيت بأسماء المحاريث","he":"הלוח הרפובליקני הצרפתי: שבועות של עשרה ימים וימים שנקראו על שם מחרשות","sw":"Kalenda ya Jamhuri ya Ufaransa: Wiki za Siku Kumi na Siku Zilizopewa Majina ya Plau"},"summary":{"en":"From 1793 to 1805 France counted years from 22 September 1792, in twelve 30-day months of three ten-day décades, with each day named for a plant, animal or tool instead of a saint. Dates such as 9 Thermidor and 18 Brumaire outlived it, and the Paris Commune briefly revived it in May 1871.","ja":"1793年から1805年まで、フランスは1792年9月22日を紀元とし、10日週3つからなる30日の月を12か月重ねる暦を使った。日々には聖人の代わりに植物・動物・農具の名が付いた。「テルミドール9日」「ブリュメール18日」といった日付は暦が廃止された後も残り、1871年5月にはパリ・コミューンがこの暦を短期間復活させた。","ko":"프랑스는 1793년부터 1805년까지 1792년 9월 22일을 기점으로 해를 셌다. 한 해는 30일짜리 열두 달, 한 달은 열흘 단위의 데카드(décade) 셋으로 이루어졌고, 날마다 성인 대신 식물·동물·도구의 이름이 붙었다. 테르미도르 9일, 브뤼메르 18일 같은 날짜는 달력 자체보다 오래 살아남았고, 1871년 5월에는 파리 코뮌이 잠시 이 달력을 되살렸다.","zh":"1793年至1805年间，法国以1792年9月22日为纪年起点，一年十二个月，每月30天，每月再分为三个十天的旬（décade），每一天都以一种植物、动物或农具命名，而不再归于某位圣人。热月9日、雾月18日这样的日期比这部历法本身流传得更久；1871年5月，巴黎公社还曾短暂恢复使用它。","yue":"1793年至1805年，法國以1792年9月22日做紀年起點，一年分十二個月，每個月30日，再分做三個十日嘅旬（décade），每日都唔再屬於某個聖人，而係用一種植物、動物或者農具嚟命名。熱月9日、霧月18日呢啲日子流傳得比呢套曆法本身仲耐；1871年5月，巴黎公社仲短暫恢復過佢。","vi":"Từ năm 1793 đến 1805, nước Pháp tính năm kể từ ngày 22 tháng 9 năm 1792, với mười hai tháng 30 ngày, mỗi tháng chia thành ba décade mười ngày, và mỗi ngày mang tên một loài cây, con vật hay nông cụ thay cho tên một vị thánh. Những ngày như 9 Thermidor và 18 Brumaire còn được nhắc đến lâu sau khi lịch bị bỏ, và Công xã Paris từng dùng lại nó trong thời gian ngắn vào tháng 5 năm 1871.","th":"ระหว่างปี 1793 ถึง 1805 ฝรั่งเศสนับปีโดยเริ่มจากวันที่ 22 กันยายน 1792 หนึ่งปีมีสิบสองเดือน เดือนละ 30 วัน แต่ละเดือนแบ่งเป็นสามเดกาด (décade) ช่วงละสิบวัน และแต่ละวันตั้งชื่อตามพืช สัตว์ หรือเครื่องมือ แทนที่จะเป็นชื่อนักบุญ วันที่อย่าง 9 แตร์มีดอร์ และ 18 บรูแมร์ ยังถูกพูดถึงต่อมาแม้ปฏิทินจะเลิกใช้ไปแล้ว และคอมมูนปารีสก็เคยนำปฏิทินนี้กลับมาใช้ชั่วคราวในเดือนพฤษภาคม 1871","id":"Dari 1793 hingga 1805, Prancis menghitung tahun sejak 22 September 1792. Setahun terdiri atas dua belas bulan 30 hari, masing-masing dibagi menjadi tiga dekade sepuluh hari, dan setiap hari dinamai menurut tumbuhan, hewan, atau perkakas, bukan menurut santo. Tanggal seperti 9 Thermidor dan 18 Brumaire tetap dikenal setelah kalender itu tidak dipakai lagi, dan Komune Paris sempat menghidupkannya kembali pada Mei 1871.","hi":"1793 से 1805 तक फ़्रांस ने अपने वर्ष 22 सितंबर 1792 से गिने: 30-30 दिनों के बारह महीने, हर महीने में दस-दस दिनों के तीन दकाद (décades), और हर दिन का नाम किसी संत के बजाय किसी पौधे, पशु या औज़ार पर। 9 थर्मिडोर और 18 ब्रूमेर जैसी तिथियाँ इस कैलेंडर से कहीं अधिक समय तक जीवित रहीं, और मई 1871 में पेरिस कम्यून ने इसे थोड़े समय के लिए फिर से अपना लिया।","de":"Von 1793 bis 1805 zählte Frankreich die Jahre ab dem 22. September 1792, in zwölf Monaten zu je 30 Tagen mit drei zehntägigen Dekaden. Statt eines Heiligen trug jeder Tag den Namen einer Pflanze, eines Tieres oder eines Werkzeugs. Daten wie der 9. Thermidor und der 18. Brumaire haben den Kalender überdauert, und die Pariser Kommune ließ ihn im Mai 1871 kurz wieder aufleben.","fr":"De 1793 à 1805, la France compta les années à partir du 22 septembre 1792, en douze mois de 30 jours divisés en trois décades. Au lieu d'un saint, chaque jour portait le nom d'une plante, d'un animal ou d'un outil. Des dates comme le 9 Thermidor et le 18 Brumaire lui ont survécu, et la Commune de Paris le fit brièvement revivre en mai 1871.","it":"Dal 1793 al 1805 la Francia contò gli anni a partire dal 22 settembre 1792, in dodici mesi di 30 giorni divisi in tre decadi. Ogni giorno portava il nome di una pianta, di un animale o di un attrezzo anziché quello di un santo. Date come il 9 termidoro e il 18 brumaio gli sono sopravvissute, e la Comune di Parigi lo riportò brevemente in vita nel maggio 1871.","es":"De 1793 a 1805, Francia contó los años a partir del 22 de septiembre de 1792, en doce meses de 30 días divididos en tres décadas de diez días. Cada día llevaba el nombre de una planta, un animal o una herramienta en lugar del de un santo. Fechas como el 9 de termidor y el 18 de brumario le sobrevivieron, y la Comuna de París lo resucitó brevemente en mayo de 1871.","pt":"De 1793 a 1805, a França contou os anos a partir de 22 de setembro de 1792, em doze meses de 30 dias divididos em três décadas de dez dias. Cada dia levava o nome de uma planta, de um animal ou de uma ferramenta em vez do de um santo. Datas como o 9 de Termidor e o 18 de Brumário sobreviveram a ele, e a Comuna de Paris o reviveu brevemente em maio de 1871.","ru":"С 1793 по 1805 год Франция вела счёт лет от 22 сентября 1792 года: двенадцать месяцев по 30 дней, в каждом три десятидневные декады, а каждый день вместо святого носил имя растения, животного или орудия труда. Такие даты, как 9 термидора и 18 брюмера, пережили сам календарь, а Парижская коммуна ненадолго возродила его в мае 1871 года.","uk":"З 1793 по 1805 рік Франція лічила роки від 22 вересня 1792 року: дванадцять місяців по 30 днів, кожен із трьох десятиденних декад, і кожен день замість святого мав назву рослини, тварини чи знаряддя праці. Такі дати, як 9 термідора і 18 брюмера, пережили сам календар, а Паризька комуна ненадовго відродила його в травні 1871 року.","ar":"من عام 1793 إلى عام 1805 عدّت فرنسا سنواتها ابتداءً من 22 سبتمبر 1792، في اثني عشر شهرًا كلٌّ منها 30 يومًا مقسَّم إلى ثلاث عُشاريات (décades) من عشرة أيام، وسُمّي كل يوم باسم نبات أو حيوان أو أداة بدلًا من اسم قدّيس. وقد عاشت تواريخ مثل 9 تيرميدور و18 برومير أطول من التقويم نفسه، وأحيته كومونة باريس لفترة وجيزة في مايو 1871.","he":"בין 1793 ל־1805 מנתה צרפת את שנותיה מ־22 בספטמבר 1792, בשנים עשר חודשים בני 30 יום, כל אחד בן שלוש דקדות של עשרה ימים, וכל יום נקרא על שם צמח, בעל חיים או כלי עבודה במקום על שם קדוש. תאריכים כמו 9 בתרמידור ו־18 בברימר האריכו ימים יותר מהלוח עצמו, וקומונת פריז החייתה אותו לזמן קצר במאי 1871.","sw":"Kuanzia 1793 hadi 1805, Ufaransa ilihesabu miaka kuanzia tarehe 22 Septemba 1792. Mwaka ulikuwa na miezi kumi na miwili ya siku 30, kila mmoja ukigawanywa katika dekadi tatu za siku kumi, na kila siku ilipewa jina la mmea, mnyama au chombo badala ya jina la mtakatifu. Tarehe kama 9 Thermidor na 18 Brumaire zimedumu kuliko kalenda yenyewe, na Komuni ya Paris iliirejesha kwa muda mfupi mwezi Mei 1871."},"body":{"en":"<h3>Year I, counted backwards</h3><p>The French Republican calendar counts its years from <strong>22 September 1792</strong>, the day after the National Convention abolished the monarchy. In Paris that day was also the autumn equinox, and the calendar's designers built the coincidence into the rules: every new year was to begin on the day of the true autumn equinox as calculated for the Paris Observatory. The scheme was decreed on 14 Vendémiaire II (5 October 1793) and given its final form on 4 Frimaire II (24 November 1793). By then Year II was already running, so no day of Year I was ever dated in the new months at the time. The year count itself was older: from 22 September 1792 public acts were dated <em>l'an premier de la République</em>, with Gregorian months, and a decree of 2 January 1793 had started Year II on 1 January 1793; the new calendar moved that start to 22 September 1793. The commission that drew it up was led by the deputy Gilbert Romme and included the mathematicians Lagrange and Monge.</p><h3>Thirty-day months, ten-day weeks</h3><p>The year had twelve months of 30 days. Each month split into three <em>décades</em>, and the days were simply numbered: <em>primidi, duodi, tridi</em>, on to <em>décadi</em>, the rest day. The five days left over at the end of the year, six in a leap year, were the <em>sansculottides</em>, festivals of Virtue, Genius, Labour, Opinion and Rewards, with a sixth, the Day of the Revolution, in leap years. A decree of 7 Fructidor III (24 August 1795) renamed them <em>jours complémentaires</em>. Because the new year followed the equinox rather than a fixed rule, leap years fell where astronomy put them: Years III, VII and XI. The map shows 22 September 1795 as <em>Jour de la Révolution, an III</em>.</p><h3>Names from the countryside</h3><p>The month names were invented by the poet and actor <strong>Fabre d'Églantine</strong> and approved on 24 October 1793. Their endings mark the season. Autumn has <em>-aire</em>: Vendémiaire (grape harvest), Brumaire (mist), Frimaire (frost). Winter has <em>-ôse</em>: Nivôse (snow), Pluviôse (rain), Ventôse (wind). Spring has <em>-al</em>: Germinal (germination), Floréal (flowers), Prairial (meadows). Summer has <em>-idor</em>: Messidor (harvest), Thermidor (heat), Fructidor (fruit). A British wit in the <em>Sporting Magazine</em> of January 1800 rendered the set as Wheezy, Sneezy, Freezy; Slippy, Drippy, Nippy; Showery, Flowery, Bowery; Hoppy, Croppy, Poppy.</p><p>The saints of the Catholic calendar were replaced as well. Fabre, helped by André Thouin, gardener at the Jardin des Plantes, gave every day a name from rural life. Every <em>quintidi</em> (the 5th, 15th and 25th) is an animal, every <em>décadi</em> a farm tool, and most of the rest are plants. In Brumaire, the 5th is <em>Oie</em> (goose) and the 10th <em>Charrue</em> (plough). Fabre did not see a full year of them in use: he was guillotined with the Dantonists on 5 April 1794, 16 Germinal II.</p><h3>Dates that became names</h3><p>On <strong>9 Thermidor II</strong> (27 July 1794), a day named for the blackberry (<em>Mûre</em>), the Convention ordered the arrest of Robespierre, who was guillotined the next day, 10 Thermidor, the day of the watering can (<em>Arrosoir</em>). The period after his fall is called the Thermidorian Reaction. On <strong>18 Brumaire VIII</strong> (9 November 1799), the day of the leadwort (<em>Dentelaire</em>), Napoleon Bonaparte began the coup that made him First Consul. Karl Marx reused the date in 1852 as the title of <em>The Eighteenth Brumaire of Louis Bonaparte</em>, about the coup of Napoleon's nephew on 2 December 1851. The map gives the two days as <em>Nonidi 9 Thermidor an II</em> and <em>Octidi 18 Brumaire an VIII</em>.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1794-07-27\" data-cal=\"french_rep\">📅 Go to 9 Thermidor II (27 July 1794)</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1799-11-09\" data-cal=\"french_rep\">📅 Go to 18 Brumaire VIII (9 November 1799)</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1871-05-06\" data-cal=\"french_rep\">📅 Go to 16 Floréal LXXIX (6 May 1871)</button></div><h3>Abolition, and a return in 1871</h3><p>Under Bonaparte the calendar was dismantled in stages. An order of 7 Thermidor VIII (26 July 1800) limited the <em>décadi</em> rest day to civil servants, and the law of 18 Germinal X (8 April 1802), which promulgated the Concordat with the Pope, moved even their rest day to Sunday. A <em>senatus-consultum</em> of 22 Fructidor XIII (9 September 1805), prepared by a commission whose report Pierre-Simon Laplace presented, restored the Gregorian calendar from 11 Nivôse XIV, which was 1 January 1806. The last Republican date in official use was <em>Décadi 10 Nivôse an XIV</em>, 31 December 1805.</p><p>The calendar came back once. In May 1871 the <em>Journal officiel</em> of the Paris Commune used Republican dates again: decrees of 6 May are dated 16 Floréal of Year LXXIX, and later issues printed the Republican date at the head of the page beside the Gregorian one. The revival is usually counted as eighteen days, from 16 Floréal to 3 Prairial (6 to 23 May). The Commune was crushed in the last week of that month.</p>"},"sources":[{"text":"Wikipedia contributors, \"French Republican calendar\", English Wikipedia (accessed 2026): commission members, 24 October 1793 adoption, Fabre and Thouin, quintidi/décadi naming, day names (Oie, Charrue, Dentelaire, Mûre, Arrosoir), leap years III/VII/XI, parody of the month names citing Sporting Magazine vol. 15 (January 1800) p. 210, Paris Commune Journal officiel 16 Floréal–3 Prairial LXXIX (18 days)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Republican_calendar"},{"text":"Contributeurs de Wikipédia, \"Calendrier républicain\", Wikipédia en français (consulté 2026): datation « l'an premier de la République » dès le 22 septembre 1792 et décret du 2 janvier 1793, décrets du 14 vendémiaire et du 4 frimaire an II, décret du 7 fructidor an III (jours complémentaires), arrêté du 7 thermidor an VIII et 18 germinal an X, sénatus-consulte du 22 fructidor an XIII et rapport de Laplace, Journal officiel de la Commune (an LXXIX)","url":"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calendrier_r%C3%A9publicain"},{"text":"Fondation Napoléon, \"The Republican calendar\", napoleon.org (Napodoc): abolition by imperial decree of 9 September 1805, Gregorian calendar resumed 1 January 1806","url":"https://www.napoleon.org/en/young-historians/napodoc/the-republican-calendar"},{"text":"Encyclopaedia Britannica, \"Philippe Fabre d'Églantine\": inventor of the month names of the calendar adopted October 1793, tried with the Dantonists and executed on 5 April 1794","url":"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Philippe-Fabre-dEglantine"}]},{"id":"maya-long-count-2012","icon":"🗿","tags":["maya","calendars","mesoamerica","epigraphy","myths"],"title":{"en":"The Maya Long Count and the World That Did Not End in 2012","ja":"マヤ長期暦と2012年：終わらなかった世界","ko":"마야 장기력과 2012년에 끝나지 않은 세계","zh":"玛雅长纪历与2012年没有终结的世界","yue":"瑪雅長紀曆，同冇喺2012年完結嘅世界","vi":"Lịch Đếm Dài của người Maya và thế giới không tận thế năm 2012","th":"ปฏิทินนับยาวของมายากับโลกที่ไม่ได้แตกในปี 2012","id":"Hitungan Panjang Maya dan Dunia yang Tidak Kiamat pada 2012","hi":"माया दीर्घ गणना और वह दुनिया जो 2012 में ख़त्म नहीं हुई","de":"Die Lange Zählung der Maya und die Welt, die 2012 nicht unterging","fr":"Le Compte long maya et le monde qui n’a pas pris fin en 2012","it":"Il Computo Lungo maya e il mondo che non finì nel 2012","es":"La Cuenta Larga maya y el mundo que no se acabó en 2012","pt":"A Contagem Longa maia e o mundo que não acabou em 2012","ru":"Длинный счёт майя и конец света, который не наступил в 2012 году","uk":"Довгий лік майя і кінець світу, якого не сталося 2012 року","ar":"العدّ الطويل عند المايا والعالم الذي لم ينتهِ عام 2012","he":"הספירה הארוכה של המאיה והעולם שלא נגמר ב־2012","sw":"Hesabu Ndefu ya Wamaya na Dunia Isiyoisha Mwaka 2012"},"summary":{"en":"On 21 December 2012 the Maya Long Count reached 13.0.0.0.0 for the first time since 3114 BCE. Neither of the two known Classic inscriptions that mention the date is a prophecy, a Palenque text counts on to 4772, and K’iche’ daykeepers have kept the 260-day count without a break.","ja":"2012年12月21日、マヤの長期暦は紀元前3114年以来はじめて13.0.0.0.0に戻った。この日付に触れる古典期の碑文は二つ知られているが、いずれも予言ではなく、パレンケの碑文は4772年まで先を数える。キチェの人々は260日の暦を途切れることなく数え続けている。","ko":"2012년 12월 21일, 마야 장기력은 기원전 3114년 이후 처음으로 13.0.0.0.0에 도달했다. 이 날짜를 언급하는 것으로 알려진 고전기 비문 두 개는 어느 쪽도 예언이 아니고, 팔렌케의 한 비문은 4772년까지 날을 세며, 키체족 날지기들은 260일 주기를 한 번도 끊지 않고 이어 왔다.","zh":"2012年12月21日，玛雅长纪历自公元前3114年以来首次走到13.0.0.0.0。已知提到这一日期的两篇古典期铭文都不是预言，帕伦克的一篇铭文一直数到4772年，而基切族守日人从未中断过260天历的计数。","yue":"2012年12月21日，瑪雅長紀曆自公元前3114年以嚟第一次行到13.0.0.0.0。已知提到呢個日子嘅兩篇古典期銘文都唔係預言，帕倫克有篇銘文一路數到4772年，而基切族嘅守日人亦從來冇停過260日曆嘅計數。","vi":"Ngày 21 tháng 12 năm 2012, Lịch Đếm Dài của người Maya lần đầu tiên chạm mốc 13.0.0.0.0 kể từ năm 3114 TCN. Cả hai văn khắc thời Cổ điển được biết có nhắc đến ngày này đều không phải lời tiên tri, một văn bản ở Palenque còn đếm tiếp tới năm 4772, và những người giữ ngày K’iche’ vẫn duy trì chu kỳ 260 ngày không hề gián đoạn.","th":"วันที่ 21 ธันวาคม ค.ศ. 2012 ปฏิทินนับยาวของมายาเดินมาถึง 13.0.0.0.0 เป็นครั้งแรกนับตั้งแต่ 3114 ปีก่อนคริสตกาล จารึกสมัยคลาสสิกสองชิ้นที่รู้จักกันซึ่งกล่าวถึงวันนี้ไม่มีชิ้นใดเป็นคำพยากรณ์ จารึกชิ้นหนึ่งที่ปาเลงเกยังนับต่อไปถึงปี 4772 และผู้รักษาวันชาวกิเชก็สืบทอดการนับ 260 วันมาโดยไม่เคยขาดตอน","id":"Pada 21 Desember 2012, Hitungan Panjang Maya mencapai 13.0.0.0.0 untuk pertama kalinya sejak 3114 SM. Tak satu pun dari dua prasasti Klasik yang diketahui menyebut tanggal itu berupa ramalan, sebuah teks Palenque terus menghitung hingga 4772, dan para penjaga hari K’iche’ memelihara hitungan 260 hari tanpa terputus.","hi":"21 दिसंबर 2012 को माया दीर्घ गणना 3114 ईसा पूर्व के बाद पहली बार 13.0.0.0.0 पर पहुँची। इस तारीख़ का ज़िक्र करने वाले दो ज्ञात क्लासिक अभिलेखों में से कोई भी भविष्यवाणी नहीं है, पालेंके का एक अभिलेख गिनती को 4772 तक ले जाता है, और किचे दिन-पालकों ने 260-दिवसीय गणना को कभी टूटने नहीं दिया।","de":"Am 21. Dezember 2012 erreichte die Lange Zählung der Maya zum ersten Mal seit 3114 v. Chr. den Stand 13.0.0.0.0. Keine der beiden bekannten klassischen Inschriften, die das Datum erwähnen, ist eine Prophezeiung, ein Text aus Palenque zählt bis 4772 weiter, und die K’iche’-Tageshüter haben die 260-Tage-Zählung ohne Unterbrechung bewahrt.","fr":"Le 21 décembre 2012, le Compte long maya a atteint 13.0.0.0.0 pour la première fois depuis 3114 av. J.-C. Aucune des deux inscriptions classiques connues qui mentionnent la date n’est une prophétie, un texte de Palenque poursuit le compte jusqu’en 4772, et les gardiens des jours k’iche’ ont tenu le compte de 260 jours sans interruption.","it":"Il 21 dicembre 2012 il Computo Lungo maya raggiunse 13.0.0.0.0 per la prima volta dal 3114 a.C. Nessuna delle due iscrizioni classiche note che citano la data è una profezia, un testo di Palenque prosegue il conto fino al 4772 e i custodi dei giorni k’iche’ hanno mantenuto senza interruzioni il computo di 260 giorni.","es":"El 21 de diciembre de 2012, la Cuenta Larga maya llegó a 13.0.0.0.0 por primera vez desde el 3114 a.C. Ninguna de las dos inscripciones clásicas conocidas que mencionan la fecha es una profecía, un texto de Palenque sigue contando hasta 4772, y los contadores de los días k’iche’ han mantenido la cuenta de 260 días sin interrupción.","pt":"Em 21 de dezembro de 2012, a Contagem Longa maia chegou a 13.0.0.0.0 pela primeira vez desde 3114 AEC. Nenhuma das duas inscrições clássicas conhecidas que mencionam a data é uma profecia, um texto de Palenque continua a contagem até 4772, e os guardiões dos dias k’iche’ mantiveram a contagem de 260 dias sem interrupção.","ru":"21 декабря 2012 года Длинный счёт майя впервые с 3114 года до н. э. достиг значения 13.0.0.0.0. Ни одна из двух известных классических надписей, где упоминается эта дата, не является пророчеством, текст из Паленке ведёт счёт до 4772 года, а хранители дней киче ни разу не прерывали 260-дневный счёт.","uk":"21 грудня 2012 року Довгий лік майя вперше від 3114 року до н. е. досяг значення 13.0.0.0.0. Жоден із двох відомих класичних написів, що згадують цю дату, не є пророцтвом, текст із Паленке веде лік до 4772 року, а хранителі днів кіче жодного разу не переривали 260-денного ліку.","ar":"في 21 ديسمبر 2012 بلغ العدّ الطويل عند المايا القيمة 13.0.0.0.0 لأول مرة منذ عام 3114 ق.م. ولا يحمل أيٌّ من النقشين الكلاسيكيين المعروفين اللذين يذكران هذا التاريخ نبوءةً، ونصٌّ من بالينكي يمضي بالعدّ إلى عام 4772، أما حفظة الأيام من شعب الكيتشي فقد واظبوا على عدّ الـ260 يومًا دون انقطاع.","he":"ב־21 בדצמבר 2012 הגיעה הספירה הארוכה של המאיה ל־13.0.0.0.0 לראשונה מאז 3114 לפנה״ס. אף אחת משתי הכתובות הקלאסיות הידועות שמזכירות את התאריך אינה נבואה, כתובת מפלנקה ממשיכה לספור עד 4772, ושומרי הימים של הקיצ'ה מקיימים את ספירת 260 הימים בלי הפסקה.","sw":"Tarehe 21 Desemba 2012, Hesabu Ndefu ya Wamaya ilifikia 13.0.0.0.0 kwa mara ya kwanza tangu 3114 KK. Hakuna hata moja kati ya maandishi mawili yanayojulikana ya kipindi cha Klasiki yanayotaja tarehe hiyo ambalo ni unabii, maandishi ya Palenque yanaendelea kuhesabu hadi 4772, na walinzi wa siku wa K’iche’ wameendeleza hesabu ya siku 260 bila kukatika."},"body":{"en":"<h3>Five places of days</h3><p>The Maya Long Count is a running total of days since a fixed base date, written in five places. One <em>k’in</em> is a day; 20 k’in make a <em>winal</em>; 18 winal make a <em>tun</em> of 360 days; 20 tun make a <em>k’atun</em> of 7,200 days; 20 k’atun make a <em>b’ak’tun</em> of 144,000 days. The count is base-20 except at the tun, where 18 keeps the unit close to a solar year. Monuments added the day’s place in the 260-day <em>tzolk’in</em> and the 365-day <em>haab’</em>.</p><p>The base date is 13.0.0.0.0 4 Ajaw 8 Kumk’u. The Goodman–Martínez–Thompson (GMT) correlation, which most Mayanists use, equates it with Julian Day Number 584,283: 11 August 3114 BCE in the proleptic Gregorian calendar. The rival constant 584,285 moves every date two days later. The oldest surviving Long Count dates come from outside the Maya area, Chiapa de Corzo Stela 2 (36 BCE) and Tres Zapotes Stela C (32 BCE); Maya kings carved them from Tikal Stela 29 (292 CE) to 10.4.0.0.0, 13 January 909 (Julian), at Toniná.</p><h3>21 December 2012</h3><p>On the base date the b’ak’tun place read 13; the next day the count restarted from 0.0.0.0.1. Thirteen b’ak’tuns are 1,872,000 days, about 5,125 years, so the b’ak’tun place reached 13 again on 21 December 2012: 13.0.0.0.0 4 Ajaw 3 K’ank’in (23 December on the 584,285 constant). The doomsday reading is modern. In the first edition of <em>The Maya</em> (1966), Michael Coe suggested that the Maya expected the world to be destroyed when the 13th b’ak’tun closed, a day he then put at 24 December 2011. José Argüelles’s <em>The Mayan Factor</em> (1987) made 21 December 2012 a date of cosmic synchronization, and books and films up to Roland Emmerich’s <em>2012</em> (2009) followed.</p><h3>What the inscriptions say</h3><p>Two known Classic texts mention the date. Tortuguero Monument 6, from Tabasco, records a building dedication by the ruler Bahlam Ajaw on 9.11.16.8.18 (11 January 669, Julian). Its last lines look ahead to the completion of the 13th b’ak’tun on 4 Ajaw 3 K’ank’in and name a god, Bolon Yokte’ K’uh. The verb is eroded: Stephen Houston and David Stuart (1996) read it as <em>descend</em>, Sven Gronemeyer and Barbara MacLeod (2010) as the god’s public display at an investiture. Stuart later concluded that the future date places a local event in time and is not a prophecy.</p><p>The second turned up in 2012 at La Corona, Guatemala, on Hieroglyphic Stairway 2. Yuknoom Yich’aak K’ahk’, king of Calakmul, visited in 696 and styled himself a <em>13 K’atun lord</em> after the k’atun ending 9.13.0.0.0 of 692; the text ties that ending to the 13th b’ak’tun. Marcello Canuto, co-director of the excavations, said in Tulane University’s announcement: “This text talks about ancient political history rather than prophecy.”</p><p>Other texts count past 2012. A panel in Palenque’s Temple of the Inscriptions projects the 80th Calendar Round (18,980 days, about 52 years) after K’inich Janaab’ Pakal’s accession to 1.0.0.0.0.8 5 Lamat 1 Mol, 21 October 4772 CE. The sixth place is the <em>piktun</em> of 20 b’ak’tuns: the b’ak’tun place was expected to run on past 13 to 19.</p><h3>The count that kept going</h3><p>The Long Count was no longer carved after the 10th century; the 260-day count was never dropped. K’iche’ daykeepers (<em>ajq’ijab’</em>) in Momostenango and other highland Guatemalan towns keep it for ceremonies, divination and naming, as Barbara Tedlock documented in <em>Time and the Highland Maya</em> (1982). Its 20 days match the Classic ones place for place under K’iche’ names: Ajpu stands where Classic texts have Ajaw. On 21 December 2012 the count stood at 4 Ajpu, and the next day at 5 Imox. New daykeepers are initiated on Wajxaqib’ B’atz’ (8 B’atz’), which recurs every 260 days: 18 January 2025, 5 October 2025, 22 June 2026, 9 March 2027.</p><p>Central Mexico kept the same count as the <em>tonalpohualli</em>, with Nahuatl day signs, until the Spanish conquest. The Caso correlation, which puts the fall of Tenochtitlan on 13 August 1521 (Julian) at 1 Coatl (1 Serpent), aligns it day for day with the Maya count: 21 December 2012 was Nahui Xochitl, 4 Flower, the sign that stands where the Maya have Ajaw.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2012-12-21\" data-cal=\"maya\">📅 Set the date to 21 December 2012 (13.0.0.0.0)</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"kiche\">🗓️ Show the K’iche’ day count</button></div>"},"sources":[{"text":"Wikipedia (2026). Mesoamerican Long Count calendar — units, GMT correlation 584,283 vs 584,285, earliest (Chiapa de Corzo St. 2, Tres Zapotes St. C, Tikal St. 29) dates, Toniná 10.4.0.0.0 (18 Jan 909 Gregorian = 13 Jan Julian), Palenque 1.0.0.0.0.8 = 21 Oct 4772, piktun.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesoamerican_Long_Count_calendar"},{"text":"Wikipedia (2026). 2012 phenomenon — Coe, The Maya (1966) and his original 24 Dec 2011 date; Argüelles, The Mayan Factor (1987); the two Classic texts that mention the 13th b’ak’tun; Gronemeyer & MacLeod (2010), ‘What Could Happen in 2012: A Re-Analysis of the 13-Bak’tun Prophecy on Tortuguero Monument 6’.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012_phenomenon"},{"text":"Tulane University / Phys.org (28 June 2012). Maya archaeologists unearth new 2012 monument (La Corona; Canuto, Barrientos, Stuart). Stairway number and 696 visit: D. Stuart, ‘Notes on a New Text from La Corona’, Maya Decipherment, 30 June 2012.","url":"https://phys.org/news/2012-06-maya-archaeologists-unearth-monument.html"},{"text":"James Doyle (2015). “The Blood Was Pooled, the Skulls Were Piled”: Maya Star Wars and a Misconstrued Doomsday. The Metropolitan Museum of Art, Perspectives (Tortuguero Monument 6; Bahlam Ajaw; dedication of 11 January 669).","url":"https://www.metmuseum.org/perspectives/tortuguero"}]},{"id":"chinese-lunisolar-solar-terms","icon":"🏮","tags":["calendar","lunisolar","china","vietnam","korea"],"title":{"en":"New Moons, Solar Terms and the Leap Month","ja":"新月と節気、そして閏月","ko":"초하루, 절기, 그리고 윤달","zh":"朔日、节气与闰月","yue":"朔日、節氣同閏月","vi":"Ngày sóc, tiết khí và tháng nhuận","th":"จันทร์ดับ ฤดูกาลย่อย และเดือนอธิกมาส","id":"Bulan Baru, Terma Surya, dan Bulan Kabisat","hi":"अमावस्या, सौर पद और अधिमास","de":"Neumonde, Sonnenperioden und der Schaltmonat","fr":"Nouvelles lunes, termes solaires et mois intercalaire","it":"Noviluni, termini solari e mese intercalare","es":"Lunas nuevas, términos solares y el mes intercalar","pt":"Luas novas, termos solares e o mês intercalar","ru":"Новолуния, солнечные сезоны и високосный месяц","uk":"Молодики, сонячні сезони та високосний місяць","ar":"القمر الجديد والمواقيت الشمسية والشهر الكبيس","he":"מולד, מועדי שמש וחודש מעובר","sw":"Mwezi Mchanga, Vipindi vya Jua na Mwezi wa Nyongeza"},"summary":{"en":"Chinese months start at the new moon, the 24 solar terms follow the Sun, and a month with no major term becomes the leap month. Korea and Vietnam use the same rules on different clocks, which in 1968 put Tết on two different days.","ja":"中国の暦では新月の日に月が始まり、二十四節気は太陽に従う。中気を含まない月が閏月になる。韓国とベトナムは同じ規則を別の時間帯で計算するので、1968年にはテトが南北で別の日になった。","ko":"중국력의 달은 초하루(삭)에 시작하고, 24절기는 태양을 따르며, 중기가 없는 달이 윤달이 된다. 한국과 베트남은 같은 규칙을 다른 표준시로 계산하는데, 그 때문에 1968년에는 뗏(Tết)이 서로 다른 두 날이 되었다.","zh":"农历的月份始于朔日，二十四节气跟随太阳，没有中气的月份就成为闰月。韩国和越南沿用同样的规则，却按不同的时区计算，结果1968年的越南春节（Tết）落在了两个不同的日子。","yue":"農曆每個月由朔日開始，二十四節氣跟住太陽行，冇中氣嘅月就變成閏月。韓國同越南用同一套規則，但按唔同時區計，結果1968年越南嘅新年（Tết）分咗兩日過。","vi":"Tháng âm lịch Trung Quốc bắt đầu vào ngày sóc, 24 tiết khí đi theo Mặt Trời, và tháng nào không có trung khí thì thành tháng nhuận. Hàn Quốc và Việt Nam dùng cùng quy tắc nhưng theo múi giờ khác, nên năm 1968 Tết rơi vào hai ngày khác nhau.","th":"เดือนในปฏิทินจีนเริ่มต้นในวันจันทร์ดับ ฤดูกาลย่อยทั้ง 24 ช่วงเดินตามดวงอาทิตย์ และเดือนที่ไม่มีฤดูกาลย่อยหลักจะกลายเป็นเดือนอธิกมาส เกาหลีและเวียดนามใช้กฎเดียวกันแต่คำนวณตามเวลาคนละเขต ซึ่งทำให้ในปี 1968 เต็ด (Tết) ตกในสองวันที่ต่างกัน","id":"Bulan-bulan dalam kalender Tionghoa dimulai saat bulan baru, 24 terma surya mengikuti Matahari, dan bulan yang tidak memuat terma utama menjadi bulan kabisat. Korea dan Vietnam memakai aturan yang sama dengan jam yang berbeda, sehingga pada 1968 Tết jatuh pada dua hari yang berlainan.","hi":"चीनी महीने अमावस्या से शुरू होते हैं, 24 सौर पद सूर्य का अनुसरण करते हैं, और जिस महीने में कोई प्रधान पद नहीं पड़ता, वह अधिमास बन जाता है। कोरिया और वियतनाम यही नियम अलग-अलग घड़ियों पर चलाते हैं, जिसके कारण 1968 में तेत दो अलग-अलग दिनों पर पड़ा।","de":"Chinesische Monate beginnen mit dem Neumond, die 24 Sonnenperioden folgen der Sonne, und ein Monat ohne Hauptperiode wird zum Schaltmonat. Korea und Vietnam wenden dieselben Regeln nach anderen Uhren an – was 1968 Tết auf zwei verschiedene Tage legte.","fr":"Les mois chinois commencent à la nouvelle lune, les 24 termes solaires suivent le Soleil, et un mois sans terme principal devient le mois intercalaire. La Corée et le Vietnam appliquent les mêmes règles sur d'autres horloges, ce qui, en 1968, a placé le Têt à deux dates différentes.","it":"I mesi cinesi iniziano con il novilunio, i 24 termini solari seguono il Sole e un mese privo di termine principale diventa il mese intercalare. Corea e Vietnam applicano le stesse regole con orologi diversi, e così nel 1968 il Tết cadde in due giorni diversi.","es":"Los meses chinos empiezan con la luna nueva, los 24 términos solares siguen al Sol y un mes sin término principal se convierte en el mes intercalar. Corea y Vietnam aplican las mismas reglas con otros relojes, lo que en 1968 situó el Tết en dos días distintos.","pt":"Os meses chineses começam na lua nova, os 24 termos solares acompanham o Sol, e um mês sem termo principal vira o mês intercalar. Coreia e Vietnã seguem as mesmas regras com outros relógios, o que em 1968 colocou o Tết em dois dias diferentes.","ru":"Месяцы китайского календаря начинаются с новолуния, 24 солнечных сезона следуют за Солнцем, а месяц, в который не попадает ни один главный сезон, становится високосным. Корея и Вьетнам пользуются теми же правилами, но по другим часам, — из-за этого в 1968 году Тет пришёлся на два разных дня.","uk":"Місяці китайського календаря починаються з молодика, 24 сонячні сезони йдуть за Сонцем, а місяць, на який не припадає жоден головний сезон, стає високосним. Корея та В'єтнам користуються тими самими правилами, але за іншим часом, — через це 1968 року Тет припав на два різні дні.","ar":"يبدأ الشهر الصيني عند القمر الجديد، وتتبع المواقيت الشمسية الأربعة والعشرون حركة الشمس، والشهر الذي لا يقع فيه أي ميقات رئيسي يصبح الشهر الكبيس. وتطبّق كوريا وفيتنام القواعد نفسها لكن بتوقيتات مختلفة، وهو ما جعل عيد تيت يقع عام 1968 في يومين مختلفين.","he":"החודש הסיני מתחיל במולד, 24 מועדי השמש עוקבים אחר השמש, וחודש שאין בו מועד עיקרי נעשה לחודש המעובר. קוריאה ווייטנאם משתמשות באותם כללים לפי שעונים אחרים, ובשנת 1968 זה הציב את טט בשני ימים שונים.","sw":"Miezi ya kalenda ya Kichina huanza na mwezi mchanga, vipindi 24 vya jua hufuata Jua, na mwezi usio na kipindi kikuu huwa mwezi wa nyongeza. Korea na Vietnam hutumia kanuni zilezile kwa saa tofauti, jambo lililoifanya Tết ya mwaka 1968 iangukie siku mbili tofauti."},"body":{"en":"<h3>A Month for the Moon, a Term for the Sun</h3><p>Each month of the Chinese calendar begins on the day of the new moon, reckoned in Beijing time (UTC+8, the 120°E meridian). A month has 29 or 30 days, and twelve of them come to about 354 days, eleven short of a solar year. Helmer Aslaksen, in <em>The Mathematics of the Chinese Calendar</em>, puts it plainly: \"Notice that the Chinese calendar is not a lunar calendar!\"</p><p>The solar half is the <strong>24 solar terms</strong> (节气 <em>jiéqì</em>), points 15° apart along the Sun's path: 立春 Beginning of Spring around 4 February, 春分 the March equinox, 冬至 the December solstice. The twelve that include the solstices and equinoxes are the major terms, 中气 <em>zhōngqì</em>. Because they follow the Sun, the terms keep almost the same Gregorian dates every year — 清明 Qingming always between 4 and 6 April — while the lunar dates move by up to a month. UNESCO inscribed the 24 solar terms as intangible cultural heritage in 2016.</p><h3>The Leap-Month Rule</h3><p>The major terms number the months: the month containing 冬至 is always the 11th, the one containing 雨水 Rain Water the 1st. On average seven times in 19 years a lunar month falls between two major terms and contains none. That month is the leap month, 闰月, and repeats the number of the month before it. The <em>Han shu</em> states the rule as 朔不得中，是謂閏月, a new moon that does not reach a major term makes a leap month, and it has applied since the Taichu calendar of 104 BCE.</p><p>What changed in 1645 was the Sun. The Shixian calendar 时宪历, compiled for the new Qing dynasty by the Jesuit Adam Schall von Bell, replaced terms spaced by the mean Sun (平气) with terms placed by the true Sun (定气). The Sun moves fastest in the northern winter, so major terms now lie 29.44 days apart in winter and 31.44 in summer, and a winter month can hold two. The modern rule, fixed in China's national standard GB/T 33661-2017, therefore takes the first month without a major term between one 11th month and the next. Leap months now fall mostly in summer. The latest was the leap sixth month of 2025, 25 July to 22 August: 大暑 Great Heat came on 22 July, in the sixth month, and 处暑 Limit of Heat on 23 August, the first day of the seventh. The year 乙巳 ran 384 days, from 29 January 2025 to 16 February 2026.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"2026-02-17\" data-cal=\"chinese\">📅 Lunar New Year 2026: 17 February</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"vietnamese\">🗓️ Show the Vietnamese lunar calendar</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"setdate\" data-date=\"1968-01-29\" data-cal=\"vietnamese\">📅 29 January 1968: Tết in Hanoi</button></div><h3>Same Rules, Other Clocks</h3><p>Korea and Vietnam use the same rules, computed for UTC+9 and UTC+7. A new moon or major term near midnight then lands on different dates. In 2012, as Park Seok-jae of the Korea Astronomy and Space Science Institute explained in the <em>Segye Ilbo</em> in 2014, the new moon that began the fifth month came at 23:02 on 19 June in China and at 0:02 on 20 June in Korea. That year Korea had a leap third month and China a leap fourth: in Korea 소만 Grain Full fell on 21 May, the first day of the fourth month, leaving the month before it with no major term. In 1985 Vietnam celebrated Tết on 21 January, China its New Year on 20 February.</p><p>In Vietnam's zodiac the fourth animal, for the branch 卯 <em>Mão</em>, is the cat (<em>mèo</em>), not the rabbit, and 丑 <em>Sửu</em> is the water buffalo (<em>trâu</em>). 2023, Quý Mão, was the Year of the Cat in Hanoi and of the Rabbit in Beijing and Seoul.</p><h3>Two Tết Dates in 1968</h3><p>On 8 August 1967 the North Vietnamese government (Decision 121/CP) fixed the North's official time at UTC+7 and approved a lunar calendar computed for that zone; the South kept the older reckoning, based on the meridian of Beijing. The new moon of Tết 1968 fell at 16:29 UTC on 29 January: 23:29 in Hanoi, so Tết there was 29 January, and 0:15 on 30 January by the old reckoning, so Saigon's Tết was 30 January. Aslaksen, citing a Vietnamese website, connects this to the Tet Offensive. The orders were to attack early on the second day of Tết; units in Da Nang and other central cities, aware of the new calendar, struck on the morning of 30 January, and Saigon and the cities to its south on 31 January.</p>"},"sources":[{"text":"Helmer Aslaksen (National University of Singapore), 'The Mathematics of the Chinese Calendar', draft of 17 July 2010 (the 'not a lunar calendar' quotation; the 1645 true-Sun reform; zhongqi spacing of 29.44–31.44 days, Table 19; the 8 August 1967 North Vietnamese lunar calendar for UTC+7; the Tết 1968 new moon at 16:29 UTC, 0:15 on 30 January in the South, and the Da Nang/Saigon attack dates, citing vietquoc.com)","url":"https://www.gwern.net/doc/science/2010-aslaksen.pdf"},{"text":"UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage, 'The Twenty-Four Solar Terms, knowledge in China of time and practices developed through observation of the sun's annual motion', inscribed 2016 (11.COM), Representative List","url":"https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/the-twenty-four-solar-terms-knowledge-in-china-of-time-and-practices-developed-through-observation-of-the-sun-s-annual-motion-00647"},{"text":"Park Seok-jae (Korea Astronomy and Space Science Institute), '[박석재의 천기누설] 올해 추석 보름달은 조금 찌그러진다', Segye Ilbo, 1 September 2014 (2012: Korea's leap 3rd month against China's leap 4th; 소만 on 21 May = 4th month day 1 in Korea; new moon 0:02 on 20 June in Korea, 23:02 on 19 June in China)","url":"https://www.segye.com/newsView/20140901004299"},{"text":"Ulrich Manthe, review of Robert H. Gassmann, Antikchinesisches Kalenderwesen (2002), Early China 29 (2004), pp. 303–321 (the leap-month rule since Taichu 1, 104 BCE; the Han shu 21a wording 朔不得中，是謂閏月)","url":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/early-china/article/robert-h-gassmann-antikchinesisches-kalenderwesen-schweizer-asiatische-studien-studienhefte-band-16-bern-peter-lang-2002-xx-454-pp/A7CF9BB1949095B9B06589CD23315370"}]},{"id":"thai-buddhist-era","icon":"🐘","tags":["thailand","buddhist era","solar calendar","new year","theravada"],"title":{"en":"Thailand's Buddhist Era and the Nine-Month Year","ja":"タイの仏暦と、9か月で終わった2483年","ko":"태국의 불기와 아홉 달짜리 한 해","zh":"泰国佛历与只有九个月的一年","yue":"泰國佛曆同得九個月嘅一年","vi":"Phật lịch Thái Lan và năm chỉ có chín tháng","th":"พุทธศักราชของไทยกับปีที่มีเพียงเก้าเดือน","id":"Era Buddha Thailand dan Tahun Sembilan Bulan","hi":"थाईलैंड का बौद्ध संवत् और नौ महीने का साल","de":"Thailands buddhistische Ära und das Jahr mit neun Monaten","fr":"L'ère bouddhique thaïlandaise et l'année de neuf mois","it":"L'era buddhista thailandese e l'anno di nove mesi","es":"La era budista de Tailandia y el año de nueve meses","pt":"A Era Budista da Tailândia e o ano de nove meses","ru":"Буддийская эра Таиланда и год длиной в девять месяцев","uk":"Буддійська ера Таїланду і рік завдовжки дев'ять місяців","ar":"التقويم البوذي في تايلاند والسنة ذات الأشهر التسعة","he":"הספירה הבודהיסטית של תאילנד והשנה בת תשעת החודשים","sw":"Enzi ya Kibuddha ya Thailand na Mwaka wa Miezi Tisa"},"summary":{"en":"Thailand counts its years from the Buddha's parinirvana, 543 years ahead of the Western count. Before that, Siam used an era of its own counted from the founding of Bangkok. In 1940 the year BE 2483 was cut to nine months to move New Year's Day to 1 January.","ja":"タイは年を仏陀の入滅から数え、西暦に543を足した数になる。仏暦の前には、バンコク遷都から数える独自の紀元を使っていた。1940年には元日を1月1日に移すため、仏暦2483年が9か月で打ち切られた。","ko":"태국은 부처의 반열반을 기점으로 해를 세며, 서력보다 543년 앞선다. 그 전에 시암은 방콕 건설을 기점으로 한 독자적인 기원을 썼다. 1940년에는 새해 첫날을 1월 1일로 옮기기 위해 불기 2483년을 아홉 달로 줄였다.","zh":"泰国以佛陀般涅槃为起点纪年，比公历早543年。在此之前，暹罗使用一种以曼谷建都为起点的本国纪元。1940年，为了把新年改到1月1日，佛历2483年被缩短为九个月。","yue":"泰國由佛陀般涅槃起計年份，比西曆早543年。喺呢之前，暹羅用過一套以曼谷建都起計嘅本國紀元。1940年，為咗將新年搬去1月1號，佛曆2483年俾人縮短到得九個月。","vi":"Thái Lan tính năm từ khi Đức Phật nhập Niết-bàn, sớm hơn cách tính phương Tây 543 năm. Trước đó, Xiêm dùng một kỷ nguyên riêng tính từ khi lập Bangkok. Năm 1940, năm Phật lịch 2483 bị rút xuống còn chín tháng để dời ngày đầu năm mới về 1 tháng 1.","th":"ไทยนับปีตั้งแต่พระพุทธเจ้าเสด็จดับขันธปรินิพพาน ซึ่งนำหน้าการนับแบบตะวันตก 543 ปี ก่อนหน้านั้นสยามเคยใช้ศักราชของตนเองที่นับจากการสถาปนากรุงเทพฯ และในปี ค.ศ. 1940 ปี พ.ศ. 2483 ถูกตัดให้เหลือเพียงเก้าเดือนเพื่อย้ายวันขึ้นปีใหม่มาเป็นวันที่ 1 มกราคม","id":"Thailand menghitung tahun sejak parinirwana Buddha, 543 tahun lebih awal daripada hitungan Barat. Sebelumnya, Siam memakai era sendiri yang dihitung sejak berdirinya Bangkok. Pada 1940, tahun BE 2483 dipangkas menjadi sembilan bulan agar Tahun Baru dapat dipindahkan ke 1 Januari.","hi":"थाईलैंड अपने वर्ष बुद्ध के परिनिर्वाण से गिनता है, जो पश्चिमी गणना से 543 वर्ष आगे है। उससे पहले स्याम में बैंकॉक की स्थापना से गिना जाने वाला उसका अपना संवत् चलता था। 1940 में बौद्ध संवत् 2483 को नौ महीने का कर दिया गया, ताकि नववर्ष 1 जनवरी को आ सके।","de":"Thailand zählt seine Jahre ab dem Parinirvana des Buddha und ist der westlichen Zählung damit um 543 Jahre voraus. Davor nutzte Siam eine eigene Ära, gerechnet ab der Gründung Bangkoks. 1940 wurde das Jahr BE 2483 auf neun Monate verkürzt, um den Neujahrstag auf den 1. Januar zu verlegen.","fr":"La Thaïlande compte ses années à partir du parinirvana du Bouddha, avec 543 ans d'avance sur le comput occidental. Auparavant, le Siam utilisait une ère qui lui était propre, comptée depuis la fondation de Bangkok. En 1940, l'année BE 2483 fut ramenée à neuf mois pour déplacer le jour de l'an au 1er janvier.","it":"La Thailandia conta gli anni a partire dal parinirvana del Buddha, con 543 anni di vantaggio sul computo occidentale. In precedenza il Siam usava un'era propria, contata dalla fondazione di Bangkok. Nel 1940 l'anno BE 2483 fu ridotto a nove mesi per spostare il Capodanno al 1º gennaio.","es":"Tailandia cuenta sus años desde el parinirvana de Buda, con 543 años de adelanto sobre el cómputo occidental. Antes, Siam usaba una era propia contada desde la fundación de Bangkok. En 1940, el año BE 2483 se recortó a nueve meses para trasladar el día de Año Nuevo al 1 de enero.","pt":"A Tailândia conta os anos a partir do parinirvana de Buda, 543 anos à frente da contagem ocidental. Antes disso, o Sião usava uma era própria, contada desde a fundação de Banguecoque. Em 1940, o ano BE 2483 foi encurtado para nove meses para mudar o dia de Ano-Novo para 1 de janeiro.","ru":"Таиланд ведёт счёт лет от паринирваны Будды — на 543 года впереди западного летосчисления. До этого в Сиаме была собственная эра, отсчитываемая от основания Бангкока. В 1940 году 2483 год буддийской эры сократили до девяти месяцев, чтобы перенести Новый год на 1 января.","uk":"Таїланд лічить роки від паринірвани Будди — на 543 роки попереду західного літочислення. Перед тим Сіам мав власну еру, яку відлічували від заснування Бангкока. 1940 року 2483 рік буддійської ери скоротили до дев'яти місяців, щоб перенести Новий рік на 1 січня.","ar":"تعدّ تايلاند سنواتها منذ بارينيرفانا بوذا، متقدّمةً بـ543 سنة على التقويم الغربي. وقبل ذلك كانت لسيام حقبة خاصة بها تبدأ من تأسيس بانكوك. وفي عام 1940 قُلِّص العام البوذي 2483 إلى تسعة أشهر لنقل رأس السنة إلى 1 يناير.","he":"תאילנד מונה את שנותיה מן הפרינירוונה של הבודהה, 543 שנים לפני הספירה המערבית. לפני כן השתמשה סיאם בספירה משלה, שנמנתה מייסוד בנגקוק. ב־1940 קוצרה שנת 2483 לספירה הבודהיסטית לתשעה חודשים, כדי להעביר את ראש השנה ל־1 בינואר.","sw":"Thailand huhesabu miaka yake tangu parinirvana ya Buddha, ikiwa mbele ya hesabu ya Kimagharibi kwa miaka 543. Kabla ya hapo, Siam ilitumia enzi yake yenyewe iliyohesabiwa tangu kuanzishwa kwa Bangkok. Mwaka 1940, mwaka BE 2483 ulifupishwa hadi miezi tisa ili kuhamisha Siku ya Mwaka Mpya hadi tarehe 1 Januari."},"body":{"en":"<p>Thailand numbers its years in the <strong>Buddhist Era</strong> (พุทธศักราช, abbreviated พ.ศ.), counted from the Buddha's parinirvana. The Thai calendar fixes the gap with the Western count at exactly 543 years, so 2026 is BE 2569. Months and days are Gregorian, and only the year number differs. On the map, 1 January 1941 reads <strong>๑ มกราคม พ.ศ. ๒๔๘๔</strong>, in Thai numerals.</p><h3>Bangkok's own era, 1889–1913</h3><p>The solar calendar is younger than the Buddhist count. Before 1889 Siam dated documents by the lunisolar calendar and the Chula Sakarat era, whose months followed the moon and needed intercalary months and days. A proclamation issued in King Chulalongkorn's name and dated Chula Sakarat 1250 (1888) replaced this system from 1 April 1889. It introduced a solar year and a new era, the <strong>Rattanakosin Era</strong> (รัตนโกสินทรศก, ร.ศ.), defined as the count of years since Bangkok became the royal capital in 1782. That first day appears on the map as <strong>๑ เมษายน ร.ศ. ๑๐๘</strong>.</p><p>The new months were named after the signs of the zodiac in Sanskrit. April, เมษายน <em>mesayon</em>, is Meṣa (Aries) plus <em>āyana</em>, \"arrival\". Thirty-day months end in <em>-ayon</em> and thirty-one-day months in <em>-akhom</em> (Sanskrit <em>āgama</em>). February, the only shorter month, ends in <em>-aphan</em>, from <em>bandha</em>, \"bound\".</p><p>King Vajiravudh dropped the era after 24 years. His proclamation, dated 21 February R.S. 131, said an era beginning in 1782 suited the present and the future but not the past, because anything older would have to be counted backward as years before the Rattanakosin Era. From 1 April 1913 the official year was BE 2456, and converting from the old era means adding 2,324. The Thai year still began in April, so 21 February R.S. 131 fell in February 1913, not 1912.</p><h3>The year that lasted nine months</h3><p>Plaek Phibunsongkhram's government moved New Year's Day from 1 April to 1 January with the Calendar Year Act of BE 2483, passed in September 1940. BE 2483 had begun on 1 April 1940 and ended on 31 December 1940, nine months later. The next day was 1 January BE 2484.</p><p>This leaves a trap in older documents. For a January, February or March date before 1941, the Western year is the BE year minus 542, not 543. A birth registered in March BE 2481 took place in March 1939.</p><h3>One Buddha, two year numbers</h3><p>Sri Lanka, Myanmar and Cambodia also use the Buddhist Era, but they start each new Buddhist year at Vesak in May, and from then until the end of the Western year their count is one ahead of Thailand's. In Sri Lanka, the Ministry of Public Administration titled its circular for the May 2025 state Vesak ceremony \"Commemoration of State Vesak Ceremony – Buddhist Era 2569\". In Thailand, 2025 was BE 2568. Cambodia called 2017 BE 2561, when Thailand called it 2560.</p><p>As a result, the 2,500th year was celebrated twice. Burma's Sixth Buddhist Council in Rangoon opened at Vesak on 17 May 1954 so that it could close at Vesak on 24 May 1956, the traditional 2,500th anniversary of the parinirvana. India held its 2,500th Buddha Jayanti celebrations the same month. Thailand marked the 25th Buddhist century in May 1957, which was BE 2500 by its count. One of the main projects for that celebration was the Phutthamonthon park at Salaya, west of Bangkok.</p><div class=\"trivia-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"buddhist\">🗓️ See the Thai solar calendar</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"trivia-action\" data-action=\"focus\" data-cal=\"rattanakosin\">🗓️ See the Rattanakosin Era</button></div>"},"sources":[{"text":"Office of the National Archives of Thailand (2016), ประกาศเปลี่ยนรัตนโกสินทรศกใช้พุทธศักราช [Proclamation changing the Rattanakosin Era to the Buddhist Era], ref. ร.6 รล 2/8 — as cited and summarised in Thai Wikipedia, 'รัตนโกสินทรศก'","url":"https://th.wikipedia.org/wiki/รัตนโกสินทรศก"},{"text":"J. C. Eade (1995), The Calendrical Systems of Mainland South-East Asia, Leiden: E. J. Brill — with the Royal Gazette text of the Calendar Year Act, B.E. 2483 (1940), as summarised in Wikipedia, 'Thai solar calendar'","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai_solar_calendar"},{"text":"Ministry of Public Administration, Sri Lanka (29 April 2025), circular 'Commemoration of State Vesak Ceremony – Buddhist Era 2569'","url":"https://pubad.gov.lk/web/images/circulars/2025/E/1746163465-haf-04-2025-e.pdf"},{"text":"Wikipedia, 'Sixth Buddhist council' (dates of opening, 17 May 1954, and closing, 24 May 1956)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixth_Buddhist_council"}]}];
